    "labs/xor-0.1.0",
    "labs/consumer-acceptance-0.1.0",
    "labs/rotating-matrices-0.1.0",
    "labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0",
]
resolver = "3"

[workspace.package]
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2024"
rust-version = "1.85"

FILE	README.md
# polytropos-alpha

Исследовательский Rust-проект для разработки **интеллектуально сильной, компактной рекуррентной LLM**. Сначала ядро должно научиться самостоятельно решать сложные **математические, химические и логические задачи**. Затем во время обучения оно должно научиться решать, какие базовые знания и навыки оставить в параметрах, а какие сохранять во **внешней иерархической латентной памяти на диске**.

**Целевые ограничения (пока не достигнуты):** уровень полезных интеллектуальных возможностей выбранного ориентира Qwen3.8 27B, **3–4 GB весов ядра**, реальное обучение на **одной RTX 5060 с 8 GB VRAM**, высокая скорость и эффективность обучения. Вращающиеся матрицы исследуются как способ сжатия параметров в **10–100 раз** при контролируемой потере качества. Целевые характеристики должны быть подтверждены экспериментами.

**Принцип разделения знаний:** ориентир **20% базовых и связующих знаний в ядре / 80% расширяемых сведений во внешней памяти**. Это не жёсткое соотношение байтов или параметров: ядро учится сохранять способности рассуждать и извлекать нужные знания. Дисковая память может расти независимо от VRAM, должна поддерживать эффективное обучение/обновление и **не загружаться в GPU целиком**. Модель запрашивает только нужные иерархические регионы и выбирает глубину погружения, например «базы данных → PostgreSQL → SQL → SELECT». В VRAM помещаются веса, обязательные вычислительные состояния и лишь ограниченное представление запрошенных данных. **Сетевые и Wiki-адаптеры пока исключены из текущего этапа.**

## Два уровня проекта

**VeriNeural** (`crates/verineural/`) — независимый от архитектуры конструктор вычислений. Пользователь определяет Rust-примитивы, операции и контракты, объединяет их в Semantic Neural IR и получает:

- LLVM NVPTX/PTX и исполнение через **CUDA Graph** на явном non-blocking stream;
- Lean 4-модели и проверку поддерживаемых математических свойств;
- артефакты перевода, проверки ограничений памяти, композиции и доверенных предположений.

VeriNeural **не поставляет готовые LLM, Transformer/Attention, KV cache или обучающий стек конкретной модели**. Они принадлежат потребительским архитектурам в `labs/` и должны собираться из публичного API. Дисковая латентная память и её обучаемая маршрутизация также относятся к конкретной LLM, а не к готовым компонентам библиотеки. Lean-доказательства математической модели не являются доказательствами CUDA JIT/SASS или успешности обучения.

## Структура

| Каталог | Назначение |
| --- | --- |
| `crates/verineural/` | Компонуемые Rust API, Semantic IR, autodiff, компиляция GPU, Lean, проверки |
| `lean/VeriNeural/` | Исходники проверяемых Lean-теорем |
| `labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/` | Исследование рекуррентной языковой модели EMA4/Torus16/Role-Delta; экспериментальная v0.2 |
| `labs/rotating-matrices-0.1.0/` | Исследование вращающихся матриц, маршрутизации, сохранённые результаты |
| `labs/xor-0.1.0/`, `labs/coupled-field-0.1.0/` | Отдельные проверяемые потребители библиотеки |
| `labs/consumer-acceptance-0.1.0/` | Приёмочные сценарии публичного API |
| `docs/verineural/` | Полная спецификация, дорожная карта, границы доказательств |

Основные документы: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) (обязательные правила и конечные критерии), [SPEC.md](docs/verineural/SPEC.md) (целевая библиотека), [ROADMAP.md](docs/verineural/ROADMAP.md) (реализованное и планы), [AUTO_BUILD.md](docs/verineural/AUTO_BUILD.md) (сертифицируемая сборка), [Torus16 v0.2 transition](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/V0.2_TRANSITION.md) и [журнал экспериментов](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/EXPERIMENT_RESULTS.md).

## Среда и основные команды

Инструменты Rust, LLVM NVPTX, CUDA toolkit, Lean 4 и Task определены в `flake.nix`. NVIDIA Driver/GPU требуются на хосте для аппаратных проверок.

```sh
nix develop
task prepare           # cargo fmt и проверка форматирования
task check             # Rust workspace (см. правило auto-format в AGENTS.md)
task test              # CPU/обычные Rust-тесты
task clippy
```

`repospool` доступен в закреплённом Nix devShell. Команда `task prepare` сначала выполняет `repospool generate .`, создавая локальный `.repospool` со снимком **закоммиченного `HEAD`** (незакоммиченные изменения не входят), затем форматирует Rust. Все основные лабораторные команды Taskfile проходят эту подготовку; `task build`, `task clippy` и `task doc` также обновляют снимок без запуска автоформатирования. Если RepoSpool завершится ошибкой, последующая лабораторная команда не запустится. Снимок является генерируемым файлом и игнорируется Git; ручной запуск: `task repospool-generate`.

Специализированные команды из единого [Taskfile.yml](Taskfile.yml):

```sh
task proof-stage3
task verify-certified-build
task lab-xor && task verify-lab-xor
task lab-stage9 && task verify-lab-stage9
task verify-gpu-temporal-bptt
task verify-gpu-batch-transfers
task test-lab-torus16-ema4-checkpoint
```

Задачи `lab-xor` и `lab-stage9` **создают проверяемые файлы в своих лабораториях** (DOT/PNG, Lean, LLVM/PTX, manifests, output bits). Эти файлы считаются **генерируемыми выходами**, в Git не хранятся. Оффлайн `verify-lab-xor` / `verify-lab-stage9` запускают **после** генерации актуального набора. Исходники и обязательства доказательств сохраняются в Rust и Lean.

Для Torus16 сначала изучить [README лаборатории](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/README.md) и [план перехода v0.2](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/V0.2_TRANSITION.md). **Полный BPTT16 GPU JIT намеренно заблокирован по умолчанию:** большой граф с 63 707 CUDA kernels зависал на загрузке драйверного модуля без нагрузки GPU. `task benchmark-torus16-v02-bptt16` исторически называется benchmark, но сейчас выполняет только безопасный **CPU preflight** без LLVM/CUDA JIT и обучения. Не считать его показателем качества модели.

## Лёгкий CI (без GPU)

GitHub Actions при push в `dev` и `main` генерирует и проверяет `.repospool`,
загружает резервный snapshot в Actions Artifacts на 7 дней, затем запускает
только `cargo test --locked -p verineural --lib --tests`. Тесты с `#[ignore]`
(требующие GPU/Lean/LLVM/Graphviz) не запускаются. **Лабораторные crates
и их задачи через CI не запускаются.** Полная GPU/Lean-приёмка остаётся локальной.

После успешных тестов workflow **коммитит `.repospool` в `dev`** отдельным
fast-forward коммитом от `github-actions[bot]` без force-push; `main` остаётся
только для чтения и тестов. Снимок содержит исходное состояние предыдущего
коммита: сам `.repospool` исключён из индекса RepoSpool, а его запись в Git
создаёт новый SHA, поэтому он не может ссылаться на собственный Git-коммит.
Следующие `task repospool-generate` / `task prepare` учитывают этот случай и
не изменяют содержимое снимка на уже опубликованном artifact-only HEAD.
Публикация выполняется только при успешной генерации, верификации и CPU-тестах;
при конкурентном push обычный fast-forward `git push` отклонит устаревший снимок.

## Правила результатов и верификации

- **Не путать** математические Lean-теоремы, структурный PTX audit, численную CUDA-проверку и неподтверждённую корректность аппаратного исполнения.
- Сообщать размер весов **отдельно** от объёма дисковой латентной памяти; измерять пик VRAM (включая состояния оптимизатора), задержки адресного чтения с диска, время компиляции/JIT, training throughput и время до качества.
- В лабораториях отделять train, validation и test; не выбирать архитектуру по зарезервированному test, сравнивать одинаковый объём обучения и учитывать различия числа optimizer updates.
- Не запускать тяжёлые GPU/Lean/Cargo задачи агентом без явного указания. Пользователь выполняет их на своей RTX 5060 и предоставляет логи.
- Рабочая ветка — только `dev`. `main` не обновляется без прямого поручения. Запрещены самовольные CI/CD и инфраструктурные сервисы.

Текущий репозиторий содержит **исследовательские реализации и проверяемые подмножества**, а не завершённую рекуррентную LLM с 3–4 GB весов и обучаемой дисковой памятью. Историю измерений хранить в профильных документах лабораторий, не раздувать корневой README очередными журналами запуска.

FILE	Taskfile.yml
version: '3'

# Local developer commands. AI agents must not execute build/test commands
# by default; see AGENTS.md. GitHub Actions checks CPU tests and publishes RepoSpool in dev.
tasks:
  default:
    desc: Show available tasks
    cmds:
      - task --list

  fmt:
    desc: Format the entire Rust workspace (developer-run)
    cmds:
      - cargo fmt --all

  repospool-generate:
    desc: Refresh the source snapshot, using its source parent after a CI artifact-only commit
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source_rev=HEAD
        if [ "$(git diff-tree --no-commit-id --name-only -r HEAD)" = ".repospool" ]; then
          source_rev=HEAD^
        fi
        repospool generate . --rev "$source_rev"

  # Safe local preflight: refresh RepoSpool, then format workspace sources.
  # Every lab generation/replay and workspace/lab test task depends on this.
  prepare:
    desc: Refresh committed-source snapshot and format Rust before laboratory runs and tests
    cmds:
      - task: repospool-generate
      - task: fmt
      - cargo fmt --all -- --check

  check:
    desc: Autoformat Rust, type-check the workspace, and publish rustfmt-only changes safely on dev
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        # Snapshot dirty source/index state before running rustfmt. Existing
        # developer edits must never become an automatic formatting commit.
        prior_rust="$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- '*.rs')"
        prior_index="$(git diff --cached --name-only)"
        task prepare
        cargo check --workspace --all-targets
        if git diff --quiet HEAD -- '*.rs'; then
          echo "check: no tracked Rust changes to publish."
          exit 0
        fi
        if [ -n "$prior_rust" ] || [ -n "$prior_index" ]; then
          echo "check: existing Rust edits or staged changes; formatted and checked, but not auto-pushing user work." >&2
          exit 0
        fi
        branch="$(git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD)" || {
          echo "check: detached HEAD; skipping automatic push." >&2
          exit 0
        }
        if [ "$branch" != "dev" ]; then
          echo "check: only dev allows automatic formatting commits (current: $branch)." >&2
          exit 0
        fi
        git diff --check
        git remote get-url origin >/dev/null
        git fetch --quiet origin dev
        remote_head="$(git rev-parse --verify refs/remotes/origin/dev)"
        if [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" != "$remote_head" ]; then
          echo "check: dev differs from origin/dev; refusing to auto-push." >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        # Tracked .rs files only. Untracked sources and existing staged work
        # are never silently added to a formatting commit.
        git add -u -- '*.rs'
        if git diff --cached --quiet; then
          echo "check: no tracked Rust changes to commit."
          exit 0
        fi
        git commit -m "style(verineural): apply cargo fmt"
        git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/dev

  build:
    desc: Build the Rust workspace (developer-run)
    deps: [repospool-generate]
    cmds:
      - cargo build --workspace

  test:
    desc: Run workspace tests (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test --workspace

  clippy:
    desc: Lint the workspace (developer-run)
    deps: [repospool-generate]
    cmds:
      - cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings

  doc:
    desc: Build Rust documentation locally (developer-run)
    deps: [repospool-generate]
    cmds:
      - cargo doc --workspace --no-deps

  example-stage2:
    desc: Run the stage-2 Semantic Neural IR example (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage2_graph

  proof-stage3:
    desc: Generate and check the stage-3 Lean 4 proof (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage3_proof

  proof-scan-invariant:
    desc: Check consumer-owned ideal-Int step claims and the bounded recurrent invariant with Lean
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example scan_invariant

  verify-inductive-invariant:
    desc: Check P1 arbitrary-horizon ideal-Int state invariant from one reusable consumer transition
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test inductive_invariant
      - cargo test -p verineural --test inductive_invariant -- --ignored

  verify-reusable-module-proof:
    desc: Check single/multi-output reusable definitions, per-instance obligations and global composition in Lean
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test reusable_module_definition
      - cargo test -p verineural --test reusable_module_definition -- --ignored

  auto-architecture:
    desc: Generate and audit all ideal-Int architecture/goal proofs and lower each supported output to NVPTX
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example auto_architecture

  verify-auto-architecture:
    desc: Offline replay of current auto-build Semantic IR, SHA-256 manifest, Lean kernel/axioms and LLVM/PTX translation
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example auto_architecture -- --verify

  proof-gated-select:
    desc: Check generic positive mask and conditional select with bounded Lean state invariant (GPU fail-closed)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example gated_select

  symbolic-shapes:
    desc: Verify two consumer symbolic-shape specializations with Lean and LLVM NVPTX (no GPU execution)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example symbolic_shapes

  verify-storage-semantics:
    desc: Check P1/P10 contiguous strides, reshape aliases and canonical storage identity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test storage_semantics
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_indexing

  gpu-multi-output:
    desc: Check one Lean model and capture/replay a shared four-output NVIDIA CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example multi_output_gpu

  verify-gpu-capabilities:
    desc: Check P1/P12 kernel-memory-translation coverage, fusion preconditions and audited Lean memory obligations
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_capability
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_capability -- --ignored
      - cargo test -p verineural --test auto_build

  gpu-state-replay:
    desc: GPU acceptance for named stateful ModelExecution, five D2D feedback steps and exact FP32 results
    deps:
      - prepare
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stateful_model_gpu

  verify-gpu-feedback-runtime:
    desc: NVIDIA regressions for raw state feedback readiness, alias snapshots and named stateful replay
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_feedback -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stateful_model_gpu

  gpu-stage4:
    desc: Lower IR to PTX and run the CUDA stage-4 example (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage4_gpu

  cert-stage5:
    desc: Run Lean, CUDA and the Stage 5 evidence bundle (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage5_cert

  verify-stage5:
    desc: Recheck Stage 5 SHA-256 manifest and Lean source (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage5_verify

  neural-stage6:
    desc: Execute Stage 6 residual FFN via Lean + CUDA and produce an evidence bundle (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage6_ffn

  gpu-stage7:
    desc: Validate fusion and benchmark reusable CUDA Graph replay with CUDA events (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage7_fusion

  verify-gpu-stage7:
    desc: Replay Stage 7 SHA-256 manifests and Lean proof checks without GPU execution (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage7_fusion -- --verify

  gpu-stage7-bench:
    desc: Benchmark four CUDA Graph workload sizes, input rebinding, and FP32 bitwise checks (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage7_benchmark --release

  numeric-stage8:
    desc: Check Stage 8 Lean/RNE and per-kernel Numeric Translation Validation before CUDA Graph execution
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage8_exact

  verify-numeric-stage8:
    desc: Offline verify Stage 8 Lean, all per-kernel LLVM/PTX translation reports, FP32 bits and SHA-256
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage8_exact -- --verify

  verify-numeric-branch:
    desc: Check P1 stable PositiveMask/SelectPositive RNE branch inheritance and fail-closed zero crossing
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test numeric_branch
      - cargo test -p verineural --test numeric_branch -- --ignored

  verify-numeric-state:
    desc: Check P1 fixed-horizon recurrent RNE contract carry and invariant state q scale
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test numeric_state
      - cargo test -p verineural --test numeric_state -- --ignored

  lab-stage9:
    desc: Build Stage 9 independent coupled-field research lab, Lean, CUDA Graph and DOT/PNG evidence
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p coupled-field-lab --example stage9_architecture

  verify-lab-stage9:
    desc: Offline reconstruct Stage 9 Semantic IR/DOT and check Lean, LLVM/PTX and SHA-256
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p coupled-field-lab --example stage9_architecture -- --verify

  lab-xor:
    desc: Check XOR MLP truth table via VeriNeural, Lean, NVPTX and CUDA Graph; write lab evidence
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p xor-lab --example xor_lab -- {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-lab-xor:
    desc: Recheck XOR lab artifacts, Lean, translation and hashes without GPU
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p xor-lab --example xor_lab -- --verify {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  certified-build:
    desc: Stage 10 certified build dispatcher for --manifest-path selected consumer (no GPU launch)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --bin cargo-verineural -- build --certified {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-certified-build:
    desc: Stage 10 offline certified replay using --manifest-path and optional external pin
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --bin cargo-verineural -- verify --certified {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-certified-stage10:
    desc: Tool-dependent Stage 10 acceptance for true/false Lean goals, identity and tamper
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test certified_build -- --ignored

  certified-xor:
    desc: Stage 10 proof-gated certified model build for XOR (CPU tools only, no GPU run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p xor-lab --example xor_certified -- {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-certified-xor:
    desc: Offline Stage 10 replay for XOR (optional --pinned-sha256 <digest>)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p xor-lab --example xor_certified -- --verify {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  certified-coupled:
    desc: Stage 10 proof-gated certified model build for CoupledField (no GPU execution)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p coupled-field-lab --example coupled_field_certified -- {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-certified-coupled:
    desc: Offline Stage 10 replay for CoupledField (optional --pinned-sha256 <digest>)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p coupled-field-lab --example coupled_field_certified -- --verify {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  test-lab-xor:
    desc: Run CPU-only XOR consumer tests including one global proof and GPU compilation planning
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p xor-lab --all-targets

  verify-relational-predicates:
    desc: Lean kernel and axiom audit acceptance for true and deliberately false consumer relational claims
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates -- --ignored

  verify-pointwise-primitive:
    desc: Kernel-check independent user-defined atomic pointwise semantics and contracts
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_primitive -- --ignored

  p0-acceptance:
    desc: Verify VN-P01..P06 supported-scope contracts, external primitive, composition and certified Lean trust boundary
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_primitive
      - cargo test -p verineural --test auto_build
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates -- --ignored
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_primitive -- --ignored
      - cargo run -p verineural --example auto_architecture
      - cargo run -p verineural --example auto_architecture -- --verify
      - cargo test -p verineural --test certified_build -- --ignored

  verify-tensor-reductions:
    desc: Lean-check axis-sum ideal semantics, nonnegative fold, and consumer contracts
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_reductions -- --ignored

  verify-tensor-slice:
    desc: Check P1 static axis slice host/IR semantics, Lean preservation and explicit GPU fail-closed
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_slice
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_slice -- --ignored

  p2-consumers:
    desc: Exercise three independent P2 consumer architectures, positive/negative contracts and honest GPU profiles
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural-consumer-acceptance --all-targets

  verify-p2-consumers:
    desc: Kernel-check P2 nested, bounded recurrent, custom primitive, tensor-heavy and deliberately false goals
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural-consumer-acceptance --all-targets -- --ignored

  verify-stage10-proof-boundary:
    desc: Stage 10 publication rollback, Lean relational composition, and GPU translation/memory fail-closed checks
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --lib interrupted_legacy_migration
      - cargo test -p verineural --lib interrupted_fresh_publication
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates -- --ignored
      - task verify-gpu-capabilities
      - task verify-certified-stage10

  verify-all-acceptance:
    desc: Developer-run combined Stage 1-4 regression, Lean, certified bundle and NVIDIA rotating acceptance
    cmds:
      - task check
      - task test
      - task clippy
      - task verify-api-acceptance
      - task verify-stage10-proof-boundary
      - task gpu-state-replay
      - task verify-lab-rotating-gpu
      - task lab-rotating

  verify-api-acceptance:
    desc: Developer-run P0/P1/P2 API contracts, real Lean checks, and independent consumer cases
    cmds:
      - task p0-acceptance
      - task verify-reusable-module-proof
      - task p2-consumers
      - task verify-p2-consumers

  verify-lab-rotating-gpu:
    desc: NVIDIA acceptance for typed ArgMax output and independent rotating-matrices CUDA Graph parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_indexing -- --ignored
      - cargo test -p rotating-matrices-lab --test gpu_parity
      - cargo test -p rotating-matrices-lab --test gpu_parity -- --ignored

  lab-rotating:
    desc: Inspect and train rotating-matrices; deterministic routing uses the unified structural/index CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --inspect
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --train 128

  inspect-lab-rotating:
    desc: Inspect rotating cores and export diagnostic Semantic IR without GPU or Lean
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --inspect

  test-lab-rotating:
    desc: Developer-run CPU tests for 40 operations, byte dictionary, rotation and IR shapes
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p rotating-matrices-lab --all-targets

  train-lab-rotating:
    desc: Train rotating cores and eight-way router with CUDA Graph and report held-out accuracy
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --train {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  certify-lab-rotating:
    desc: Build rotating-matrices structural/index evidence with Lean and NVPTX (no GPU launch)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --certify-architecture

  lab-torus16-mix:
    desc: Inspect the VeriNeural Torus16-Mix operator and execute the Tensor host reference
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example torus16_mix -- --inspect

  inspect-ir-torus16-mix:
    desc: Print the complete canonical Torus16-Mix operator Semantic IR
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example torus16_mix -- --ir

  test-lab-torus16-mix:
    desc: Run Torus16-Mix plus reusable one-row structural GPU contract tests (no PyTorch)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test structural_last_row
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_gpu
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab

  verify-gpu-structural-last-row:
    desc: Run ignored NVIDIA acceptance for generic SliceAxis/BroadcastTo/Concat(1) in one CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test structural_last_row -- --ignored --nocapture

  lab-torus16-mix-gpu:
    desc: Run all eight Torus16-Mix roles in one CUDA Graph with explicit approximate exp and compare Tensor oracle
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example torus16_mix -- --gpu

  verify-gpu-torus16-mix:
    desc: NVIDIA GPU acceptance for Torus16-Mix full multi-output forward (no PyTorch)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test gpu_forward -- --ignored --nocapture

  pointwise-binary-chain-fusion:
    desc: Structural checks for generic two-operation Add/Mul CUDA fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test binary_pointwise_fusion

  verify-gpu-binary-chain-fusion:
    desc: NVIDIA bitwise parity for opt-in two-operation Add/Mul fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test binary_pointwise_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  pointwise-three-op-fusion:
    desc: Structural contracts for three-op strict FP32 pointwise CUDA fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_mul_fusion

  verify-gpu-three-op-fusion:
    desc: NVIDIA bitwise equivalence for twelve Mul-Add-Mul operand layouts
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_mul_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  pointwise-mul-add-fusion:
    desc: Validate checked opt-in Mul+Add CUDA fusion and its reverse-mode boundaries
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_fusion

  verify-gpu-mul-add-fusion:
    desc: NVIDIA bitwise fused vs unfused Mul-then-Add parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  temporal-bptt-stage:
    desc: Test generic recurrent IR unroll, through-time dependency and full EMA4 parameter inventory
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test temporal
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4

  verify-gpu-temporal-bptt:
    desc: Verify a two-step recurrent gradient with a hand-derived NVIDIA CUDA oracle
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test temporal -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-batch-transfers:
    desc: NVIDIA acceptance for partial H2D updates, selective batched D2H and old API parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_batch_transfers -- --ignored --nocapture

  test-lab-torus16-ema4-checkpoint:
    desc: CPU round-trip, corruption rejection and AdamW restart continuity for EMA4 snapshots
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib ema4_checkpoint -- --nocapture

  train-lab-torus16-ema4-bptt:
    desc: Release-optimized BPTT with batched transfers and per-stage wall-clock profiling
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt

  verify-gpu-p2-equivalence:
    desc: NVIDIA P2 acceptance - D2D/host feedback, fused/unfused FP32, EMA4 uninterrupted vs checkpoint resume
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_feedback -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_mul_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo test -p verineural --test binary_pointwise_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture
      - |
        set -eu
        # Never read, overwrite or resume the user's normal training file.
        parity_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/verineural-ema4-p2.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$parity_dir"; else printf "P2 logs/checkpoints retained at %s\n" "$parity_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2
        echo "P2 (1/3): full EMA4 fused/unfused parity, then two training windows"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/first.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/first.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q '^fusion_parity=PASS .*scope=EMA4_logits_gradients_terminal_states$' "$parity_dir/first.log"
        grep -q '^train_window=1 .*optimizer_step=2 ' "$parity_dir/first.log"
        echo "P2 (2/3): resume the two-window checkpoint to four windows"
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/resume.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/resume.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q '^checkpoint_resumed=.*completed_windows=2$' "$parity_dir/resume.log"
        grep -q '^train_window=3 .*optimizer_step=4 ' "$parity_dir/resume.log"
        echo "P2 (3/3): continuous four-window training from a fresh initialization"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/continuous.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/continuous.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/continuous.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q '^train_window=3 .*optimizer_step=4 ' "$parity_dir/continuous.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/first.log" >"$parity_dir/observed.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/resume.log" >>"$parity_dir/observed.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/continuous.log" >"$parity_dir/expected.log"
        if ! cmp -s "$parity_dir/observed.log" "$parity_dir/expected.log"; then
          echo "FAIL: per-window EMA4 CE/BPC or optimizer step differs" >&2
          diff -u "$parity_dir/expected.log" "$parity_dir/observed.log" || true
          exit 1
        fi
        if ! cmp -s "$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" "$parity_dir/continuous.ckpt"; then
          echo "FAIL: checkpoint differs (parameters, recurrent states, AdamW, cursor)" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        echo "PASS: EMA4 fused/unfused logits, gradients and terminal states match at FP32 bit level"
        echo "PASS: uninterrupted and checkpoint-resumed training match per-window CE/BPC and optimizer steps"
        echo "PASS: final EMA4 checkpoints are bit-identical, including 271 parameter tensors, recurrent states and AdamW"

  verify-gpu-kernel-reuse:
    desc: Validate NVPTX specialization interning, translation evidence, and NVIDIA CUDA Graph parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test kernel_specialization_reuse
      - cargo test -p verineural --test kernel_specialization_reuse -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-dual-pointwise-outputs:
    desc: Check observable dual-output RNE fusion with structural tests and NVIDIA CUDA Graph parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test dual_pointwise_outputs
      - cargo test -p verineural --test dual_pointwise_outputs -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-diamond-fusion:
    desc: Structural and NVIDIA bitwise acceptance for four-op rounded diamond fusion with selected output
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_diamond_add_fusion
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_diamond_add_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-four-op-fusion:
    desc: Structural and NVIDIA bitwise acceptance for generic rounded four-operation pointwise fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_mul_add_div_fusion
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_mul_add_div_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-sqrt-add-div-fusion:
    desc: Structural and NVIDIA bitwise acceptance for generic 3-operation rounded Sqrt/Add/Div fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test sqrt_add_div_fusion
      - cargo test -p verineural --test sqrt_add_div_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-independent-batch:
    desc: NVIDIA accept independent CUDA Graph session preparation, pending IO guard, and bitwise serial/parallel equivalence
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_independent_batch independent_replay_matches_serial_and_rejects_pending_access -- --ignored --nocapture

  benchmark-gpu-independent-batch:
    desc: Measure four independent CUDA Graphs serial vs queued on separate non-blocking streams
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_independent_batch independent_streams_report_serial_vs_queued_wall_time -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-adamw:
    desc: Experimental generic CUDA Graph AdamW, host numeric oracle, GPU restart and EMA4 checkpoint parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_adamw
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_adamw -- --ignored --nocapture
      - |
        set -eu
        parity_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/verineural-gpu-adamw.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$parity_dir"; else printf "GPU AdamW logs and checkpoint retained at %s\n" "$parity_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/first.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/first.log"; exit 1; }
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/resume.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/resume.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q '^checkpoint_resumed=.*completed_windows=2$' "$parity_dir/resume.log"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/continuous.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/continuous.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/continuous.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q 'optimizer_backend=GPU_IR$' "$parity_dir/continuous.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/first.log" >"$parity_dir/observed.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/resume.log" >>"$parity_dir/observed.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/continuous.log" >"$parity_dir/expected.log"
        diff -u "$parity_dir/expected.log" "$parity_dir/observed.log"
        cmp "$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" "$parity_dir/continuous.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: GPU AdamW 4-step checkpoint/resume matches uninterrupted training bit-for-bit"
        echo "PASS: GPU AdamW original parameters and optimizer moments survive checkpoint/resume"

  benchmark-torus16-holdout-reuse:
    desc: Compare fresh and reused holdout GPU sessions, requiring exact validation, test and checkpoint parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        bench_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/torus16-holdout.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$bench_dir"; else printf "Holdout logs and checkpoints retained at %s\n" "$bench_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_BPTT TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE TORUS16_ROLE_INIT TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=64 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=64 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32
        for mode in fresh reused; do
          printf '\nholdout_mode=%s\n' "$mode"
          if [ "$mode" = reused ]; then export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1; else unset TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT; fi
          TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/$mode.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/$mode.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/$mode.log"; exit 1; }
          grep '^holdout_session_mode=' "$bench_dir/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/$mode.log"
          grep '^validation_window=' "$bench_dir/$mode.log"
        done
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p; /^validation_window=/s/ elapsed_s=.*$//p; /^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=/s/ eval_score_seconds=.*$//p; /^test_reset_streaming_bpc=/s/ checkpoint=.*$//p' "$bench_dir/fresh.log" >"$bench_dir/fresh.metrics"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p; /^validation_window=/s/ elapsed_s=.*$//p; /^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=/s/ eval_score_seconds=.*$//p; /^test_reset_streaming_bpc=/s/ checkpoint=.*$//p' "$bench_dir/reused.log" >"$bench_dir/reused.metrics"
        diff -u "$bench_dir/fresh.metrics" "$bench_dir/reused.metrics"
        cmp "$bench_dir/fresh.ckpt" "$bench_dir/reused.ckpt"
        cmp "$bench_dir/fresh.best.ckpt" "$bench_dir/reused.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: fresh and reused holdout BPC/checkpoints match bit-for-bit"
        echo "NOTE: holdout_session_prepare_s is one-time setup outside training clock"

  benchmark-torus16-codegen:
    desc: Compare strict-FP32 NVPTX llc O0/O2 on GPU AdamW, fail closed on PTX translation and checkpoint mismatch
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        bench_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/torus16-codegen.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$bench_dir"; else printf "Codegen logs and checkpoints retained at %s\n" "$bench_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_BPTT TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE TORUS16_ROLE_INIT TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32
        for opt in 0 2; do
          printf '\nllc_codegen_optimization=-O%s\n' "$opt"
          TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT="$opt" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/opt$opt.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/opt$opt.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/opt$opt.log"; exit 1; }
          grep '^llc_codegen_optimization=' "$bench_dir/opt$opt.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/opt$opt.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$bench_dir/opt$opt.log"
        done
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$bench_dir/opt0.log" >"$bench_dir/opt0.curve"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$bench_dir/opt2.log" >"$bench_dir/opt2.curve"
        diff -u "$bench_dir/opt0.curve" "$bench_dir/opt2.curve"
        cmp "$bench_dir/opt0.ckpt" "$bench_dir/opt2.ckpt"
        cmp "$bench_dir/opt0.best.ckpt" "$bench_dir/opt2.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: O2 matches O0 sample-by-sample and preserves final and best checkpoints bit-for-bit"
        echo "NOTE: O2 remains experimental; rerun benchmarks to confirm speed and use a separate resume regression"

  benchmark-torus16-throughput:
    desc: GPU AdamW throughput tuning; compare optional sparse loss readback and CUDA block size, require bitwise checkpoint parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        bench_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/torus16-throughput.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$bench_dir"; else printf "Benchmark logs retained at %s\n" "$bench_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_BPTT TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE TORUS16_ROLE_INIT TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        for choice in "256 1" "256 32" "64 32" "128 32" "512 32"; do
          set -- $choice
          threads="$1"; metric_every="$2"
          label="${threads}_${metric_every}"
          printf '\nthreads=%s metric_every=%s\n' "$threads" "$metric_every"
          TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK="$threads" TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY="$metric_every" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/$label.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/$label.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/$label.log"; exit 1; }
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/$label.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$bench_dir/$label.log"
          grep '^cuda_graph_before=' "$bench_dir/$label.log"
        done
        cmp "$bench_dir/256_1.ckpt" "$bench_dir/256_32.ckpt"
        cmp "$bench_dir/256_1.best.ckpt" "$bench_dir/256_32.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: metric sampling preserves parameters, optimizer moments, states and validation selection bit-for-bit"
        echo "NOTE: compare tokens/s, not nvidia-smi utilisation; different block sizes require their own NVIDIA parity check"

  benchmark-gpu-adamw:
    desc: Compare sustained host/GPU AdamW throughput on the same EMA4 four-layer BPTT graph (256 windows)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        bench_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/verineural-adamw-bench.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$bench_dir"; else printf "Benchmark logs retained at %s\n" "$bench_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE TORUS16_ROLE_INIT TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=128 TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED=1
        echo "Benchmark: host AdamW (256 windows)"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/host.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/host.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/host.log"; exit 1; }
        echo "Benchmark: GPU IR AdamW (256 windows; finite-domain D2H validation)"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/device.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/gpu.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/gpu.log"; exit 1; }
        echo "Host result:"
        grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/host.log"
        grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$bench_dir/host.log"
        grep '^fused_cuda_graph_event_average_ms=' "$bench_dir/host.log"
        grep '^cuda_graph_before=' "$bench_dir/host.log"
        echo "GPU result:"
        grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"
        grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"
        grep '^fused_cuda_graph_event_average_ms=' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"
        grep '^cuda_graph_before=' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"
        if ! grep -Eq '^cuda_graph_before=.* diamond_fusions=[1-9][0-9]* ' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"; then
          echo "FAIL: GPU AdamW did not activate the required observable-output diamond fusion" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        echo "NOTE: end-to-end throughput is authoritative; GPU optimizer adds IR kernels and may be slower."

  verify-torus16-matrix-initial:
    desc: NVIDIA bitwise parity between independently initialized W and Torus16-Mix tied W, before training (Rust only)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 torus_matrix_modes_initial_gpu_logits_and_state_match_bits -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-torus16-matrix-gradients:
    desc: "NVIDIA numerical VJP check: shared W gradient equals sum of eight independent role gradients"
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 torus_role_matrix_gradients_sum_to_shared_gradient -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-torus16-matrix-training:
    desc: Full 2-step BPTT, fused/unfused GPU gradient parity, AdamW, and exact independent/shared checkpoint-resume
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/vn-matrix-train-test.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$dir"; else echo "GPU training test logs at $dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched
        for mode in torus_shared independent; do
          export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode"
          TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH="$dir/$mode.initial-probe" \
            TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/$mode-resumed.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/$mode-start.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 80 "$dir/$mode-start.log"; exit 1;
            }
          grep -q '^fusion_parity=PASS ' "$dir/$mode-start.log"
          TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/$mode-resumed.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/$mode-resume.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 80 "$dir/$mode-resume.log"; exit 1;
            }
          TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/$mode-continuous.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/$mode-continuous.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 80 "$dir/$mode-continuous.log"; exit 1;
            }
          cmp "$dir/$mode-resumed.ckpt" "$dir/$mode-continuous.ckpt"
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$dir/$mode-resume.log"
          grep '^test_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$dir/$mode-resume.log"
          echo "PASS: $mode two-step BPTT/GPU AdamW parity and bitwise resume"
        done
        cmp "$dir/torus_shared.initial-probe" "$dir/independent.initial-probe"
        echo "PASS: initial training BPTT logits and terminal states bitwise-equal across architectures"

  finetune-torus16-best-lr5:
    desc: Paired seed-0 best-checkpoint continuation with 5x reduced AdamW LR and preserved moments
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        # Match checkpoint fingerprints: BPTT, validation frequency and
        # training budget are set as one consistent preset, not independent
        # inherited environment variables. BPTT=2 remains the default.
        bptt="${TORUS16_FINETUNE_BPTT:-2}"
        case "$bptt" in
          2)
            source_default=target/torus16-pilot
            out_default=target/torus16-finetune-lr5-seed0
            eval_every=2048
            checkpoint_every=1024
            default_windows=98304
            ;;
          4)
            source_default=target/torus16-bptt4-seed0
            out_default=target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0
            eval_every=1024
            checkpoint_every=512
            default_windows=65536
            ;;
          *) echo "TORUS16_FINETUNE_BPTT must be 2 or 4" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        source_dir="${TORUS16_FINETUNE_SOURCE_DIR:-$source_default}"
        out="${TORUS16_FINETUNE_DIR:-$out_default}"
        if [ "$source_dir" = "$out" ]; then echo "Source and finetune directories must differ" >&2; exit 1; fi
        mkdir -p "$out"
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X=1 TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_BPTT="$bptt"
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=512 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=512 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY="$eval_every" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY="$checkpoint_every"
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        export TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS="${TORUS16_FINETUNE_WINDOWS:-$default_windows}"
        for mode in torus_shared independent; do
          tag="$mode-matched-seed0"
          source_best="$source_dir/$tag.best.ckpt"
          destination="$out/$tag.ckpt"
          best="$out/$tag.best.ckpt"
          log="$out/$tag.log"
          if [ ! -f "$source_best" ]; then echo "Missing source best checkpoint: $source_best" >&2; exit 1; fi
          if [ ! -e "$destination" ] && [ ! -e "$best" ]; then
            cp "$source_best" "$destination"
            cp "$source_best" "$best"
          elif [ ! -f "$destination" ] || [ ! -f "$best" ]; then
            echo "Incomplete finetune checkpoint pair: $destination / $best" >&2
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "Fine-tune: $tag bptt=$TORUS16_BPTT target_windows=$TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS AdamW_LR=0.0004 (best-checkpoint source)"
          TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode" TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0 \
            TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$destination" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >>"$log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$log"
              echo "FAIL: $tag; full log at $log" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^checkpoint_resumed=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_adamw_lr=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^test_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^validation_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.validation_curve.log"
          grep '^train_curve_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.train_curve.log"
        done
        echo "PASS: paired seed-0 finetune completed, logs/checkpoints: $out"

  compare-torus16-matrix-tying:
    desc: Resumable seeded Rust/VeriNeural Torus16-Mix LM ablation with train/validation curves
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        unset TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        out="${TORUS16_MATRIX_ABLATION_DIR:-target/torus16-matrix-ablation}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_BPTT="${TORUS16_BPTT:-2}"
        export TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS="${TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS:-65536}"
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT="${TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT:-4096}"
        export TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT="${TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT:-4096}"
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY="${TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY:-8192}"
        export TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY="${TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY:-4096}"
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1
        # Default is one paired matched-W seed. Set MATRIX_SEEDS="1 2 3"
        # for replicate trials, INCLUDE_DIVERSE=1 for the independent-W
        # baseline, and MATRIX_ABLATION_FRESH=1 for an explicit fresh run.
        if [ "${TORUS16_MATRIX_ABLATION_FRESH:-0}" = 1 ]; then
          export TORUS16_FRESH=1
        else
          unset TORUS16_FRESH
        fi
        for seed in ${TORUS16_MATRIX_SEEDS:-0}; do
          case "$seed" in ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "Invalid uint64 seed: $seed" >&2; exit 1;; esac
          variants="torus_shared:matched independent:matched"
          if [ "${TORUS16_INCLUDE_DIVERSE:-0}" = 1 ]; then
            variants="$variants independent:diverse"
          fi
          for variant in $variants; do
            mode="${variant%%:*}"
            init="${variant#*:}"
            tag="$mode-$init-seed$seed"
            log="$out/$tag.log"
            echo "Torus16-Mix training: $tag (windows=$TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS, BPTT=$TORUS16_BPTT, validation=$TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT)"
            if [ -n "${TORUS16_FRESH:-}" ] || [ ! -f "$out/$tag.ckpt" ]; then
              : >"$log"
            fi
            TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode" TORUS16_ROLE_INIT="$init" TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED="$seed" \
              TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$tag.ckpt" \
              cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >>"$log" 2>&1 || {
                tail -n 100 "$log"
                echo "FAIL: $tag; full log in $log" >&2
                exit 1
              }
            grep '^experiment_matrix_mode=' "$log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^training_total_s=' "$log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^test_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^train_curve_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.train_curve.log"
            grep '^validation_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.validation_curve.log"
          done
        done
        echo "PASS: matched-seed Torus16-Mix pair evaluated; results at $out"
        echo "best checkpoints: $out/*.best.ckpt"

  autodiff-stage:
    desc: Validate architecture-neutral reverse-mode IR rules, finite difference checks and atomic AdamW
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test autodiff

  verify-gpu-autodiff:
    desc: Validate reverse-mode MatMul/fanout gradients through CUDA Graph against independent oracle
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test autodiff -- --ignored --nocapture

  train-lab-torus16-ema4:
    desc: GPU CE to reverse-IR VJP to host AdamW, one-token truncated gradient for final-beta only
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_train

  lab-torus16-ema4:
    desc: Inspect the 4-layer streaming EMA4-LM architecture built from VeriNeural primitives
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4 -- --inspect

  test-lab-torus16-ema4:
    desc: Validate research-sized parameter count, all named states and causal CPU reference
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_gpu
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4

  lab-torus16-ema4-gpu:
    desc: Execute three EMA4-LM autoregressive steps through one persistent CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4 -- --gpu

  verify-gpu-torus16-ema4:
    desc: NVIDIA acceptance for streaming EMA4-LM logits and on-device EMA feedback
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 -- --ignored --nocapture

  certify-lab-torus16-mix:
    desc: Fail closed on unsupported certified numerical semantics of pointwise Exp/Div
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example torus16_mix -- --certify


  verify-torus16-role-delta:
    desc: Validate Role-Delta inventory, scalar gradients, initial EMA4 parity and projection GPU VJP
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 role_delta_parameter_inventory_and_zero_adapter_initialization
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib role_delta_scalar_vjp_matches_finite_differences
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib role_delta_parameter_only_hoisting_reduces_real_bptt_ir -- --nocapture
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib role_delta_warm_start_accepts_shared_and_rejects_incompatible_sources
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 role_delta_initial_gpu_logits_and_state_match -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib role_delta_gpu_vjp_matches_scalar_oracle -- --ignored --nocapture

  compare-torus16-role-delta-ranks:
    desc: Paired rank-4/rank-8 validation-only Role-Delta experiments (resumable, no test peeking)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing TorusShared source checkpoint: $source (set TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE)" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        backend="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_BACKEND:-cpu}"
        case "$backend" in
          cpu)
            default_out=target/torus16-role-delta-rank-ablation
            unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT
            export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1
            ;;
          gpu)
            default_out=target/torus16-role-delta-rank-ablation-gpu
            export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32 TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1
            ;;
          *) echo "TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_BACKEND must be cpu or gpu" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        out="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_DIR:-$default_out}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1
        export TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_WINDOWS:-8192}"
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=512 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=512
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=1024 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=512
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SEED:-0}"
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        unset TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED
        unset TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH
        unset TORUS16_CORPUS
        for mode in role_delta_4 role_delta_8; do
          tag="$mode-seed$TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED"
          log="$out/$tag.log"
          if [ ! -f "$out/$tag.ckpt" ]; then : >"$log"; fi
          echo "Role-Delta validation-only ablation: $tag backend=$backend, windows=$TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS, source=$source"
          TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$tag.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >>"$log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$log"
              echo "FAIL: $tag; see $log" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^experiment_matrix_mode=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^validation_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.validation_curve.log" || true
          grep '^train_curve_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.train_curve.log" || true
        done
        echo "Compare best_validation_bpc from both ranks; the test suffix has not been evaluated."
        echo "Checkpoints, logs and curves: $out"

  verify-torus16-role-delta-resume:
    desc: Bitwise checkpoint/resume versus continuous Role-Delta training, with test held out
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing TorusShared source checkpoint: $source (set TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE)" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        mode="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_VERIFY_MODE:-role_delta_4}"
        case "$mode" in
          role_delta_2|role_delta_4|role_delta_8) ;;
          *) echo "Unsupported Role-Delta mode: $mode" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        mkdir -p target
        dir="$(mktemp -d target/torus16-role-delta-resume.XXXXXX)"
        echo "Resume evidence directory: $dir"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode" TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2 TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        unset TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_FRESH
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/start.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/start.log"; exit 1;
          }
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/resume.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/resume.log"; exit 1;
          }
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/continuous.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/continuous.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/continuous.log"; exit 1;
          }
        grep -q '^checkpoint_resumed=' "$dir/resume.log"
        for log in "$dir/start.log" "$dir/resume.log" "$dir/continuous.log"; do
          grep -q '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$log"
        done
        cmp "$dir/resumed.ckpt" "$dir/continuous.ckpt"
        cmp "$dir/resumed.best.ckpt" "$dir/continuous.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: $mode bitwise checkpoint/resume and validation-best checkpoint"
        echo "Evidence: $dir"

  benchmark-torus16-role-delta-backends:
    desc: Compare CPU/GPU optimizer throughput for warm-start rank4 BPTT4
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then echo "Missing warm-start source: $source" >&2; exit 1; fi
        out="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-role-delta-backend-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        # A benchmark must not accidentally resume a previous trial.
        export TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED
        unset TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        for backend in cpu gpu; do
          if [ "$backend" = gpu ]; then
            export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32 TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1
          else
            unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT
            export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1
          fi
          echo "Role-Delta BPTT4 throughput backend=$backend windows=256"
          TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$backend.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$backend.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$backend.log"
              echo "FAIL: backend=$backend log=$out/$backend.log" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^cuda_graph_' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
        done
        echo "Compare training_tokens_per_second, profile and compilation costs; utilization alone is insufficient."
        echo "CPU/GPU checkpoints are separate; numerical parity between optimizers is not assumed."
        echo "Evidence: $out"

  verify-torus16-role-delta-fast-setup:
    desc: Bitwise CPU Role-Delta checkpoint parity with and without redundant unfused compilation
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then echo "Missing warm-start source: $source" >&2; exit 1; fi
        mkdir -p target
        dir="$(mktemp -d target/torus16-role-delta-fast-setup.XXXXXX)"
        echo "Fast-setup evidence directory: $dir"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2 TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        export TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        unset TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED
        unset TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=0 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/baseline.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/baseline.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/baseline.log"; exit 1;
          }
        TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/fast.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/fast.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/fast.log"; exit 1;
          }
        grep -q '^cuda_graph_before=' "$dir/baseline.log"
        grep -q '^cuda_graph_baseline=SKIPPED ' "$dir/fast.log"
        grep -q '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$dir/fast.log"
        cmp "$dir/baseline.ckpt" "$dir/fast.ckpt"
        cmp "$dir/baseline.best.ckpt" "$dir/fast.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: fast setup and full diagnostic setup produce bitwise-identical checkpoints"
        echo "Original preparation:"
        grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$dir/baseline.log"
        echo "Fast preparation:"
        grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$dir/fast.log"
        echo "Evidence: $dir"

  profile-torus16-bptt16-interning:
    desc: CPU BPTT16 preflight; opt-in NVIDIA BPTT8/BPTT16 JIT and synchronized CUDA Graph probes (no training)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        gpu="${TORUS16_PROFILE_RUN_GPU:-0}"
        case "$gpu" in 0|1) ;; *) echo "TORUS16_PROFILE_RUN_GPU must be 0 or 1" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
        out="${TORUS16_PROFILE_BPTT_DIR:-target/torus16-bptt16-interning}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt bptt16_budget_tests -- --nocapture
        # No warm-start, training, validation, test, or checkpoint mutation.
        unset TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW
        unset TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED
        unset TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=1 TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=1
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_TENSOR_MIB=512
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_UNIQUE_KERNELS=4096
        export VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE=1
        export TORUS16_BPTT=16 TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY=1
        unset TORUS16_BPTT16_ENABLE_SLOW_JIT
        # Preflight never calls LLVM llc or CUDA, even when the budget fails.
        TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/never-written-bptt16.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/bptt16-preflight.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 80 "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"; exit 1;
          }
        grep '^gpu_compilation_inventory bptt=16 ' "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"
        grep '^bptt16_resource_preflight ' "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"
        grep -F 'bptt16_preflight_only=PASS cuda_jit=SKIPPED gpu_graph=NOT_CREATED training=SKIPPED validation=SKIPPED test=SKIPPED' "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"
        if grep -Eq '^(gpu_nvptx_stage=|gpu_prepare_phase=|setup_probe=|training_total_s=)' "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"; then
          echo "FAIL: preflight entered GPU work or training" >&2; exit 1
        fi
        if [ "$gpu" = 0 ]; then
          echo "PASS: BPTT16 CPU-only inventory. NVIDIA probes withheld."
          echo "Explicit opt-in: TORUS16_PROFILE_RUN_GPU=1 task profile-torus16-bptt16-interning"
          echo "Logs: $out"
          exit 0
        fi
        timeout_s="${TORUS16_PROFILE_TIMEOUT_S:-240}"
        case "$timeout_s" in ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "TORUS16_PROFILE_TIMEOUT_S must be integer seconds" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
        if [ "$timeout_s" -lt 30 ] || [ "$timeout_s" -gt 900 ]; then
          echo "TORUS16_PROFILE_TIMEOUT_S must be in 30..900" >&2; exit 1
        fi
        export TORUS16_SETUP_PROBE_ONLY=1 TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY=0
        # Raise the separate graph-node cap only for this explicitly opted-in
        # diagnostic. PTX entrypoint and graph-tensor caps remain independent.
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_KERNELS=80000
        for bptt in 8 16; do
          export TORUS16_BPTT="$bptt"
          if [ "$bptt" -eq 16 ]; then
            export TORUS16_BPTT16_ENABLE_SLOW_JIT=1
          else
            unset TORUS16_BPTT16_ENABLE_SLOW_JIT
          fi
          label="bptt$bptt-probe"
          echo "NVIDIA setup/replay probe $label (timeout=${timeout_s}s, no AdamW/checkpoint/validation)"
          TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/never-written-$label.ckpt" \
            timeout -k 10s "${timeout_s}s" cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$label.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$label.log"
              echo "FAIL: $label; JIT may be too large; artifacts: $out" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep "^setup_probe=PASS bptt=$bptt " "$out/$label.log"
          grep '^gpu_nvptx_stage=' "$out/$label.log"
          grep '^gpu_prepare_phase=' "$out/$label.log"
          if [ -e "$out/never-written-$label.ckpt" ]; then
            echo "FAIL: setup probe modified checkpoint" >&2; exit 1
          fi
        done
        echo "PASS: two GPU setup probes completed. CUDA event replay and JIT timings are diagnostic, not throughput/BPC results."
        echo "Graph tensor bytes are NOT peak VRAM. Evidence: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-v02-bptt16:
    desc: SAFE BPTT16 graph preflight only; never start blocking driver PTX JIT or a CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        # Compatibility with the old task name. The previous task generated
        # 63,707 CUDA kernels and hung in CUDA module loading with no GPU load.
        # This task now does CPU graph analysis ONLY, not GPU benchmarking.
        base="${TORUS16_V02_BPTT16_DIR:-target/torus16-v02-bptt16-preflight}"
        mkdir -p "$base"
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY=1
        export TORUS16_V02_RANKS=4 TORUS16_V02_BPTTS=16
        export TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS=64 TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS=64
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_KERNELS=40000
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_TENSOR_MIB=512
        unset TORUS16_BPTT16_ENABLE_SLOW_JIT
        echo "BPTT16 safety: CPU-only resource preflight, no CUDA driver JIT, no training or evaluation."
        TORUS16_V02_DIR="$base" task benchmark-torus16-v02-horizon >"$base/summary.log" 2>&1 || {
          tail -n 120 "$base/summary.log"
          echo "FAIL: BPTT16 preflight; logs under $base" >&2
          exit 1
        }
        raw="$base/rank4-bptt16.log"
        grep '^bptt16_resource_preflight ' "$raw"
        grep -Fx 'bptt16_preflight_only=PASS cuda_jit=SKIPPED gpu_graph=NOT_CREATED training=SKIPPED validation=SKIPPED test=SKIPPED' "$raw"
        if grep -Eq '^(gpu_nvptx_stage=|gpu_prepare_phase=|training_total_s=)' "$raw"; then
          echo "FAIL: BPTT16 preflight unexpectedly entered LLVM/CUDA or training" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        echo "PASS: CPU-only BPTT16 preflight completed without launching CUDA JIT."
        echo "GPU replay NOT RUN: use TORUS16_PROFILE_RUN_GPU=1 task profile-torus16-bptt16-interning for an explicitly bounded diagnostic."
        echo "Logs: $base/summary.log $raw"

  benchmark-torus16-v02-allocation-slab:
    desc: Compare separate CUDA tensor allocations against a single bounded slab and require bitwise checkpoint parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        base="${TORUS16_V02_SLAB_DIR:-target/torus16-v02-allocation-slab}"
        mkdir -p "$base"
        export VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE=1
        export TORUS16_V02_RANKS=4 TORUS16_V02_BPTTS=8
        export TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS=64 TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS=64
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ALLOCATION_SLAB
        for mode in separate slab; do
          if [ "$mode" = slab ]; then
            export TORUS16_GPU_ALLOCATION_SLAB=1
          else
            unset TORUS16_GPU_ALLOCATION_SLAB
          fi
          echo "v0.2 memory layout=$mode role_delta_4 BPTT8 (64-char setup smoke)"
          TORUS16_V02_DIR="$base/$mode" task benchmark-torus16-v02-horizon >"$base/$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$base/$mode.log"
            exit 1
          }
          # The nested task prints only a summary. Allocation details
          # exist in the raw training log, not in the nested task stdout.
          raw="$base/$mode/rank4-bptt8.log"
          if [ ! -s "$raw" ]; then
            echo "Missing raw training log: $raw" >&2
            exit 1
          fi
          grep -Fx "gpu_allocation_mode=$mode" "$raw" || {
            echo "Unexpected GPU allocation mode in $raw" >&2
            tail -n 100 "$raw"
            exit 1
          }
          grep "^gpu_prepare_allocations mode=$mode .*artifact_dir=.*vn_ema4_bptt_" "$raw"
          grep '^gpu_prepare_phase=.*artifact_dir=.*vn_ema4_bptt_' "$raw"
          grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$raw"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$raw"
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$raw"
        done
        cmp "$base/separate/rank4-bptt8.ckpt" "$base/slab/rank4-bptt8.ckpt"
        cmp "$base/separate/rank4-bptt8.best.ckpt" "$base/slab/rank4-bptt8.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: slab and separate CUDA allocations preserve final/best checkpoint bits."
        echo "DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: 64-char validation must not be used to rank architecture quality."
        echo "Summary logs: $base/separate.log $base/slab.log"
        echo "Raw GPU logs: $base/separate/rank4-bptt8.log $base/slab/rank4-bptt8.log"

  benchmark-torus16-v02-setup-stability:
    desc: Repeat BPTT8 CUDA setup across fresh processes, report phase spread and verify deterministic checkpoint bytes
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        base="${TORUS16_V02_SETUP_DIR:-target/torus16-v02-setup-stability}"
        mkdir -p "$base"
        export VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE=1
        export TORUS16_V02_RANKS=4 TORUS16_V02_BPTTS=8
        export TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS=64 TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS=64
        for trial in 1 2 3; do
          echo "CUDA setup reproducibility trial=$trial/3, role_delta_4 BPTT8, separate process"
          TORUS16_V02_DIR="$base/trial$trial" task benchmark-torus16-v02-horizon >"$base/trial$trial.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$base/trial$trial.log"
            exit 1
          }
          # Distinguish the training graph from the much smaller reused
          # holdout graph. Report stages without collapsing them into one timer.
          grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          grep '^gpu_nvptx_stage=.*artifact_dir=.*vn_ema4_bptt_' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          grep '^gpu_prepare_phase=.*artifact_dir=.*vn_ema4_bptt_' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          if [ "$trial" != 1 ]; then
            cmp "$base/trial1/rank4-bptt8.ckpt" "$base/trial$trial/rank4-bptt8.ckpt"
            cmp "$base/trial1/rank4-bptt8.best.ckpt" "$base/trial$trial/rank4-bptt8.best.ckpt"
          fi
        done
        echo "PASS: checkpoint bits identical across three independent setup runs."
        echo "DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: 64-char validation is not an architecture quality gate."
        echo "Compare llc, cuda_module_load, kernel_resolution and graph_instantiate across trials."
        echo "Logs: $base/trial1.log $base/trial2.log $base/trial3.log"

  benchmark-torus16-v02-horizon:
    desc: v0.2 transition gate - Role-Delta rank 4/8 x BPTT 4/8 with packed I/O and long validation
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing TorusShared warm-start checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        # Equal training characters, NOT equal optimizer updates.
        train_tokens="${TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS:-4096}"
        case "$train_tokens" in
          ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS must be an integer" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        if [ "$train_tokens" -lt 8 ] || [ "$train_tokens" -gt 32768 ] || [ "$((train_tokens % 8))" -ne 0 ]; then
          echo "TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS must be 8..32768 and divisible by 8" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        # Long-validation acceptance remains the default. A 64-character
        # diagnostic mode is useful only for compiler/setup profiling.
        validation_chars="${TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS:-8192}"
        case "$validation_chars" in
          64|8192) ;;
          *) echo "TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS must be 64 (setup smoke) or 8192 (acceptance)" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        out="${TORUS16_V02_DIR:-target/torus16-v02-horizon}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0 TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT="$validation_chars" TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=8192
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=16
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        export TORUS16_PACKED_D2H=1 TORUS16_PACKED_H2D=1 TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=1
        export TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=1024
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        # Default is the full matrix. Filter specific configurations when
        # investigating expensive CUDA setup, without touching other runs.
        ranks="${TORUS16_V02_RANKS:-4 8}"
        bptts="${TORUS16_V02_BPTTS:-4 8}"
        for rank in $ranks; do
          case "$rank" in 4|8) ;; *) echo "Invalid v0.2 rank: $rank" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
          for bptt in $bptts; do
            case "$bptt" in 4|8|16) ;; *) echo "Invalid v0.2 BPTT: $bptt" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
            if [ "$((train_tokens % bptt))" -ne 0 ]; then
              echo "Training tokens ($train_tokens) must be divisible by BPTT=$bptt" >&2
              exit 1
            fi
            windows="$((train_tokens / bptt))"
            export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="role_delta_$rank"
            export TORUS16_BPTT="$bptt" TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS="$windows"
            # Evaluate only after the same number of trained characters.
            export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY="$windows"
            label="rank$rank-bptt$bptt"
            echo "v0.2 gate $label training_characters=$train_tokens windows=$windows validation_characters=$validation_chars"
            TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$label.ckpt" \
              cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$label.log" 2>&1 || {
                tail -n 100 "$out/$label.log"
                echo "FAIL: v0.2 gate $label ($out/$label.log)" >&2
                exit 1
              }
            # A BPTT16 CPU-only inspection returns successfully before
            # llc and cuModuleLoadData. Do not require training metrics or
            # final/best checkpoints from a preflight-only execution.
            if [ "$bptt" -eq 16 ] && [ "${TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY:-0}" = 1 ]; then
              grep '^bptt16_resource_preflight ' "$out/$label.log"
              grep '^bptt16_preflight_only=PASS ' "$out/$label.log"
              echo "BPTT16 training=SKIPPED because this is CPU-only JIT preflight."
              continue
            fi
            grep '^temporal_parameter_only_hoisting=enabled ' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^cuda_graph_baseline=SKIPPED ' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            if [ -n "${VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE:-}" ]; then
              grep '^gpu_nvptx_stage=' "$out/$label.log"
              grep '^gpu_prepare_phase=' "$out/$label.log"
            fi
            grep '^training_parameter_upload_mode=packed_true' "$out/$label.log"
            grep '^training_d2h_profile_avg_ms .*packed=true' "$out/$label.log"
            grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep "^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=.*scored_characters=$validation_chars " "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
          done
        done
        if [ "${TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY:-0}" = "1" ]; then
          echo "PASS: BPTT16 CPU-only graph inspection finished; training/validation/test and CUDA JIT were NOT run."
        else
          echo "PASS: selected runs completed, validation_characters=$validation_chars, test withheld."
        fi
        if [ "$validation_chars" != 8192 ]; then
          echo "DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: validation is too short to rank architectures."
        fi
        echo "Important: BPTT changes optimizer update count; different ranks/BPTT have different checkpoint identities."
        echo "Evidence and checkpoints: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-packed-hoisting:
    desc: Paired and reversed-order BPTT hoisting benchmark with both packed CUDA Graph transfers enabled
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_PACKED_HOIST_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-packed-hoist-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        export TORUS16_PACKED_D2H=1 TORUS16_PACKED_H2D=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        for trial in 1 2; do
          # Reverse order to expose first-run/warm-cache and driver variation.
          if [ "$trial" = 1 ]; then modes="baseline hoisted"; else modes="hoisted baseline"; fi
          for mode in $modes; do
            if [ "$mode" = hoisted ]; then hoist=1; else hoist=0; fi
            echo "packed BPTT4 trial=$trial mode=$mode, 256 windows"
            TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY="$hoist" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$trial-$mode.ckpt" \
              cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$trial-$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
                tail -n 100 "$out/$trial-$mode.log"
                exit 1
              }
            grep '^temporal_parameter_only_hoisting=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^cuda_graph_baseline=SKIPPED ' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^setup_stage=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log"
            grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^training_parameter_upload_mode=packed_true' "$out/$trial-$mode.log"
            grep '^training_d2h_profile_avg_ms .*packed=true' "$out/$trial-$mode.log"
            grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          done
        done
        for mode in baseline hoisted; do
          cmp "$out/1-$mode.ckpt" "$out/2-$mode.ckpt"
          cmp "$out/1-$mode.best.ckpt" "$out/2-$mode.best.ckpt"
        done
        echo "PASS: each IR mode is deterministic across both trials; compare modes by replay/throughput/BPC."
        echo "Different IR fingerprints and FP32 reduction order: do NOT compare hoisted vs baseline checkpoint bytes."
        echo "Measurements: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-packed-h2d:
    desc: Compare packed parameter H2D versus standard CPU AdamW upload and check checkpoint bits
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_PACKED_H2D_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-packed-h2d-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=0
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        export TORUS16_PACKED_D2H=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_PACKED_H2D
        for mode in baseline packed; do
          if [ "$mode" = packed ]; then export TORUS16_PACKED_H2D=1; else unset TORUS16_PACKED_H2D; fi
          echo "CPU AdamW upload=$mode, rank4 BPTT4, 256 windows, packed D2H"
          TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$mode.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$mode.log"
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^training_parameter_upload_mode=' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$mode.log"
        done
        cmp "$out/baseline.ckpt" "$out/packed.ckpt"
        cmp "$out/baseline.best.ckpt" "$out/packed.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: packed H2D preserves exact CPU AdamW checkpoint bits"
        echo "Logs and checkpoints: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-packed-d2h:
    desc: Compare standard CPU AdamW D2H against CUDA Graph packed gradient readback and verify checkpoint bits
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_PACKED_D2H_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-packed-d2h-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=0
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_PACKED_D2H TORUS16_PACKED_H2D
        for mode in baseline packed; do
          if [ "$mode" = packed ]; then export TORUS16_PACKED_D2H=1; else unset TORUS16_PACKED_D2H; fi
          echo "CPU AdamW readback=$mode, rank4 BPTT4, 256 windows"
          TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$mode.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$mode.log"
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^training_d2h_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$mode.log"
        done
        cmp "$out/baseline.ckpt" "$out/packed.ckpt"
        cmp "$out/baseline.best.ckpt" "$out/packed.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: packed CUDA Graph readback preserves exact CPU AdamW checkpoint bits"
        echo "Logs and checkpoints: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-cpu-metric-sampling:
    desc: Verify CPU AdamW metric sampling preserves rank-4 BPTT-4 checkpoints bit-for-bit and profile D2H
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_CPU_METRIC_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-cpu-metric-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=0
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        for every in 1 16; do
          echo "CPU AdamW metric sample=$every, rank4 BPTT4, 256 windows"
          TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY="$every" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/metric$every.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/metric$every.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/metric$every.log"
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^training_d2h_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/metric$every.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/metric$every.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/metric$every.log"
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/metric$every.log"
        done
        cmp "$out/metric1.ckpt" "$out/metric16.ckpt"
        cmp "$out/metric1.best.ckpt" "$out/metric16.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: sampled CPU logits preserve full optimizer/state/checkpoint bits"
        echo "Compare repeated throughput and separate D2H enqueue/sync/host-copy timings, not one noisy run."
        echo "Logs and checkpoints: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-role-delta-hoisting:
    desc: Compare same rank-4 BPTT-4 training with and without parameter-only temporal IR reuse
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_HOIST_DIR:-target/torus16-role-delta-hoist-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        for mode in baseline hoisted; do
          if [ "$mode" = hoisted ]; then hoist=1; else hoist=0; fi
          echo "Temporal parameter-only reuse: $mode, rank4 BPTT4, 256 windows"
          TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY="$hoist" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$mode.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$mode.log"
              echo "FAIL: $mode, log=$out/$mode.log" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^temporal_parameter_only_hoisting=' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^cuda_graph_baseline=SKIPPED ' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^setup_stage=' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
        done
        echo "Assess kernel count, replay time, wall-clock throughput and validation BPC."
        echo "Different IR fingerprints/FP32 gradient reduction order: do not require bitwise checkpoint equality."
        echo "Logs and checkpoints: $out"

FILE	crates/verineural/Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "verineural"
version.workspace = true
edition.workspace = true
rust-version.workspace = true
description = "Importable Rust library for neural computation and formal verification (Semantic IR, Lean proof, and experimental LLVM NVPTX/CUDA stage)"
publish = false

[lib]
name = "verineural"
path = "src/lib.rs"

# Stage 4 still has no Rust dependencies; NVIDIA driver is loaded dynamically.
# llc is supplied by flake.nix, and GPU execution requires a system NVIDIA driver.

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/auto_architecture.rs
//! Independent architecture consumer: define reusable local modules, wire a
//! fork/fan-in graph, then verify all selected outputs and a global goal and
//! emit NVPTX without manually invoking either backend for each component.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    ArchitectureAutoCompiler, ArchitectureProofTask, ContractClaim, Domain, GpuRequirement,
    MathContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NeuralModule, NodeId, PortContract, ProofGoal,
    ProofGoalKind, Shape,
};

struct Activated {
    contract: MathContract,
}
impl NeuralModule for Activated {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "consumer_activation"
    }
    fn semantic_version(&self) -> &'static str {
        "1.0"
    }
    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
        &self.contract
    }
    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.relu(inputs[0])
    }
}

struct Merge {
    contract: MathContract,
}
impl NeuralModule for Merge {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "consumer_merge"
    }
    fn semantic_version(&self) -> &'static str {
        "1.0"
    }
    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
        &self.contract
    }
    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.add(inputs[0], inputs[1])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let args = std::env::args().skip(1).collect::<Vec<_>>();
    let pinned = match args.as_slice() {
        [] => None,
        [command] if command == "--verify" => None,
        [command, option, digest] if command == "--verify" && option == "--pinned-sha256" => {
            Some(digest.as_str())
        }
        _ => {
            return Err(
                "usage: auto_architecture [--verify [--pinned-sha256 <64-hex-digest>]]".into(),
            );
        }
    };
    let verify = !args.is_empty();
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![4])?;
    let finite = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let nonnegative = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let any = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Any);
    let activated = Activated {
        contract: MathContract::new(vec![finite], nonnegative.clone())
            .with_claim(ContractClaim::Nonnegative),
    };
    let merge = Merge {
        contract: MathContract::new(vec![nonnegative.clone(), nonnegative], any)
            .with_claim(ContractClaim::Nonnegative),
    };

    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let signal = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let parameter = graph.input(shape, Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let left = graph.apply_module(&activated, &[signal])?;
    let right = graph.apply_module(&activated, &[parameter])?;
    let output = graph.apply_module(&merge, &[left, right])?;

    let tasks = vec![
        ArchitectureProofTask::Goal(ProofGoal {
            name: "merged_nonnegative".to_owned(),
            output,
            kind: ProofGoalKind::Nonnegative {
                assumptions: Vec::new(),
            },
        }),
        ArchitectureProofTask::Goal(ProofGoal {
            name: "left_nonnegative".to_owned(),
            output: left,
            kind: ProofGoalKind::Nonnegative {
                assumptions: Vec::new(),
            },
        }),
    ];
    let compiler = ArchitectureAutoCompiler::default();
    let root = Path::new("target/verineural/auto-architecture");
    let outputs = [left, right, output];
    let report = if verify {
        compiler.verify_bundle(
            &graph,
            &outputs,
            &tasks,
            GpuRequirement::AllOutputs,
            root,
            pinned,
        )?
    } else {
        compiler.build(&graph, &outputs, &tasks, GpuRequirement::AllOutputs, root)?
    };
    println!(
        "Wiring: {} edges, {} bound module ports, {} instances; \
         checked {} architecture theorems and {} independent goal(s)",
        report.connectivity.data_edges,
        report.connectivity.module_ports,
        report.connectivity.module_instances,
        report.architecture_theorems,
        report.goal_theorems.len(),
    );
    for artifact in &report.output_evidence {
        println!("GPU output {}: {:?}", artifact.node, artifact.ptx);
    }
    println!("Report: {}", report.directory.join("report.txt").display());
    println!(
        "SHA256SUMS digest (pin externally): {}",
        report.manifest_sha256
    );
    if verify && pinned.is_none() {
        println!(
            "Provenance: unpinned replay checks current Rust IR and all bundle contents, not external authenticity"
        );
    }
    println!(
        "Assurance: Lean ideal-Int and structural PTX translation only; GPU machine semantics not proven"
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/gated_select.rs
//! Consumer-defined gated state update over generic mask and selection IR.
//! Produces a Lean-checked fixed-horizon ideal-Int invariant, while binary32
//! RNE and NVPTX lowering remain explicitly unsupported for these new ops.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    ContractClaim, Domain, GpuEngine, GpuError, LeanProofEngine, MultiOutputContract,
    MultiOutputModule, NamedPortContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NodeId, PortContract, Shape,
    Tensor,
};

struct GatedUpdate {
    interface: MultiOutputContract,
}

impl MultiOutputModule for GatedUpdate {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "consumer_gated_update"
    }
    fn contract(&self) -> &MultiOutputContract {
        &self.interface
    }
    fn semantic_version(&self) -> &'static str {
        "1.0"
    }

    fn build(
        &self,
        graph: &mut NeuralGraph,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError> {
        let mask = graph.positive_mask(inputs[1])?;
        let next_state = graph.select_positive(mask, inputs[1], inputs[0])?;
        let readout = graph.relu(next_state)?;
        Ok(vec![next_state, readout])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![3])?;
    let positive = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let named = |name| NamedPortContract::new(name, positive.clone());
    let module = GatedUpdate {
        interface: MultiOutputContract {
            inputs: vec![named("state"), named("input")],
            outputs: vec![
                NamedPortContract {
                    name: "next_state",
                    port: positive.clone(),
                    claims: vec![ContractClaim::Nonnegative],
                },
                named("output"),
            ],
        },
    };

    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let initial = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let first = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let second = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let scan = graph.scan_fixed(&module, initial, &[first, second])?;
    let checker = LeanProofEngine::default();
    let lean = checker.generate_fixed_scan_nonnegative(&graph, &scan, "gated")?;
    let file = Path::new("target/verineural/verification/gated_select.lean");
    let (checked, audit) = checker.verify_certified(&lean, file)?;

    // An independent concrete host-reference fixture, not an FP32 theorem.
    let mask = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![-1.0f32, 0.0, f32::NAN])?;
    let yes = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![1.0, 2.0, 3.0])?;
    let no = Tensor::new(shape, vec![4.0, 5.0, 6.0])?;
    assert_eq!(mask.positive_mask().values(), &[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]);
    assert_eq!(mask.select_positive(&yes, &no)?.values(), &[4.0, 5.0, 6.0]);

    for output in &scan.outputs {
        assert!(matches!(
            GpuEngine::default().compile(&graph, *output),
            Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation { .. })
        ));
    }
    println!(
        "Lean checked {} theorems (H=2); assumptions={}; axioms={:?}",
        checked.theorem_names.len(),
        checked.assumptions.len(),
        audit
            .axiom_dependencies
            .values()
            .flatten()
            .collect::<std::collections::BTreeSet<_>>()
    );
    println!(
        "Assurance: ideal-Int bounded invariant; f32 mask reference checked; RNE/GPU lowering unsupported"
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/multi_output_gpu.rs
//! One CUDA Graph computes four declared outputs with one shared producer.
//! Lean certifies only the ideal-Int model, not NVIDIA FP32 machine behavior.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{Domain, GpuEngine, LeanProofEngine, NeuralGraph, Shape, Tensor};

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![4])?;
    let x = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let y = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let common = graph.add(x, y)?;
    let activated = graph.relu(common)?;
    let weighted = graph.mul(common, y)?;
    let output = graph.add(activated, weighted)?;
    let outputs = [common, activated, weighted, output];
    let gpu = GpuEngine::default();
    let shared = gpu.compile_outputs(&graph, &outputs)?;
    let independent = outputs
        .iter()
        .map(|&id| gpu.compile(&graph, id)?.kernel_count())
        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?
        .into_iter()
        .sum::<usize>();
    println!(
        "Shared CUDA Graph: {} kernels vs {} independently compiled kernels",
        shared.kernel_count()?,
        independent
    );
    assert_eq!(shared.kernel_count()?, 4);
    assert!(independent > 4);

    let proof = LeanProofEngine::default().generate_outputs(&graph, &outputs)?;
    let lean = Path::new("target/verineural/multi-output-gpu/multi_output.lean");
    let (checked, axiom_audit) = LeanProofEngine::default().verify_certified(&proof, lean)?;
    println!(
        "Lean checked {} ideal-Int statements, audited {} theorem dependencies",
        checked.theorem_names.len(),
        axiom_audit.axiom_dependencies.len()
    );

    let input = |id, data| Tensor::new(shape.clone(), data).map(|value| (id, value));
    let inputs = [
        input(x, vec![1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0])?,
        input(y, vec![2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0])?,
    ];
    let dir = Path::new("target/verineural/multi-output-gpu/shared");
    let mut execution = gpu.prepare(&shared, &inputs, dir)?;
    execution.replay()?;
    let observed = execution.read_outputs()?;
    let expected: [&[f32]; 4] = [
        &[3.0, 5.0, 7.0, 9.0],
        &[3.0, 5.0, 7.0, 9.0],
        &[6.0, 15.0, 28.0, 45.0],
        &[9.0, 20.0, 35.0, 54.0],
    ];
    for ((id, tensor), (expected_id, oracle)) in
        observed.iter().zip(outputs.iter().zip(expected.iter()))
    {
        assert_eq!(id, expected_id);
        assert_eq!(tensor.values(), *oracle);
    }

    // Replay the exact same captured kernel DAG with a new input batch.
    let changed = [
        input(x, vec![1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0])?,
        input(y, vec![1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0])?,
    ];
    execution.update_inputs(&changed)?;
    execution.replay()?;
    let changed_outputs = execution.read_outputs()?;
    let next_expected: [&[f32]; 4] = [
        &[2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0],
        &[2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0],
        &[2.0, 6.0, 12.0, 20.0],
        &[4.0, 9.0, 16.0, 25.0],
    ];
    for ((id, tensor), (expected_id, oracle)) in changed_outputs
        .iter()
        .zip(outputs.iter().zip(next_expected.iter()))
    {
        assert_eq!(id, expected_id);
        assert_eq!(tensor.values(), *oracle);
    }
    println!("CUDA Graph captured once, replayed twice; four outputs match exact FP32 fixtures.");
    println!(
        "Assurance: conditional ideal-Int Lean; structurally validated PTX; concrete GPU bits tested, not formally proved."
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/scan_invariant.rs
//! Consumer-defined fixed-horizon recurrence with independently checked
//! ideal-Int local claims and a global nonnegative state invariant.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    ContractClaim, Domain, LeanProofEngine, MultiOutputContract, MultiOutputModule,
    NamedPortContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NodeId, PortContract, Shape,
};

struct Accumulate {
    contract: MultiOutputContract,
}

impl MultiOutputModule for Accumulate {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "consumer_accumulate"
    }

    fn contract(&self) -> &MultiOutputContract {
        &self.contract
    }

    fn build(
        &self,
        graph: &mut NeuralGraph,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError> {
        // The f32 domain of additions stays Any: they can overflow. The
        // mathematical ideal-Int property is proved separately by Lean.
        let next = graph.add(inputs[0], inputs[1])?;
        let output = graph.relu(next)?;
        Ok(vec![next, output])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![2])?;
    let any = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Any);
    let transition = Accumulate {
        contract: MultiOutputContract {
            inputs: vec![
                NamedPortContract::new("state", any.clone()),
                NamedPortContract::new("input", any.clone()),
            ],
            outputs: vec![
                NamedPortContract {
                    name: "next_state",
                    port: any.clone(),
                    claims: vec![ContractClaim::Nonnegative],
                },
                NamedPortContract::new("output", any),
            ],
        },
    };
    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let initial = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let x0 = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let x1 = graph.input(shape, Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let scan = graph.scan_fixed(&transition, initial, &[x0, x1])?;
    let proof =
        LeanProofEngine::default().generate_fixed_scan_nonnegative(&graph, &scan, "accumulator")?;
    let output = Path::new("target/verineural/verification/scan_invariant.lean");
    let (checked, audit) = LeanProofEngine::default().verify_certified(&proof, output)?;
    println!(
        "Lean certified {} theorems in {}; bounded horizon {}, conditional source hypotheses {}, reviewed axioms {:?}",
        checked.theorem_names.len(),
        checked.path.display(),
        scan.outputs.len(),
        checked.assumptions.len(),
        audit
            .axiom_dependencies
            .values()
            .flatten()
            .collect::<std::collections::BTreeSet<_>>(),
    );
    println!(
        "Assurance: ideal-Int bounded invariant only; no FP32, GPU or unbounded induction proof"
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stage2_graph.rs
//! Stage-2 example: Rust modules produce checked symbolic IR, not GPU code.
use verineural::{
    Domain, MathContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NeuralModule, NodeId, PortContract, Shape,
    Tensor,
};

struct PositiveLayer {
    contract: MathContract,
}

impl NeuralModule for PositiveLayer {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "positive_layer"
    }

    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
        &self.contract
    }

    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.relu(inputs[0])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![2, 2])?;
    let input_values = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![-1.0f32, 4.0, 9.0, 16.0])?;
    // This independently checks the assumption used to construct the IR source.
    input_values.validate_domain(Domain::Finite)?;

    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let input = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let positive = PositiveLayer {
        contract: MathContract::new(
            vec![PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite)],
            PortContract::new(shape, Domain::NonNegativeFinite),
        ),
    };
    let hidden = graph.apply_module(&positive, &[input])?;
    let output = graph.sqrt(hidden)?;

    let expected = input_values.relu().sqrt()?;
    assert_eq!(expected.values(), &[0.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0]);
    println!(
        "IR nodes: {}, output: {:?}",
        graph.nodes().len(),
        graph.node(output)?.shape
    );
    println!("Host reference output: {:?}", expected.values());
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stage3_proof.rs
//! End-to-end Stage 3: build Rust IR, emit Lean 4, check all proof obligations.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    Domain, LeanProofEngine, MathContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NeuralModule, NodeId,
    PortContract, Shape,
};

struct ReluLayer {
    contract: MathContract,
}

impl NeuralModule for ReluLayer {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "relu"
    }

    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
        &self.contract
    }

    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, input: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.relu(input[0])
    }
}

struct Flatten {
    contract: MathContract,
}

impl NeuralModule for Flatten {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "flatten"
    }

    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
        &self.contract
    }

    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, input: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.reshape(input[0], Shape::new(vec![4])?)
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let square = Shape::new(vec![2, 2])?;
    let flat = Shape::new(vec![4])?;

    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let input = graph.input(square.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let relu = ReluLayer {
        contract: MathContract::new(
            vec![PortContract::new(square.clone(), Domain::Finite)],
            PortContract::new(square.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite),
        ),
    };
    let flatten = Flatten {
        contract: MathContract::new(
            vec![PortContract::new(square, Domain::NonNegativeFinite)],
            PortContract::new(flat, Domain::NonNegativeFinite),
        ),
    };

    let hidden = graph.apply_module(&relu, &[input])?;
    let reshaped = graph.apply_module(&flatten, &[hidden])?;
    let square = graph.mul(reshaped, reshaped)?;
    let output = graph.add(square, reshaped)?;

    let engine = LeanProofEngine::default();
    let generated = engine.generate(&graph, output)?;
    let file = Path::new("target/verineural/verification/stage3.lean");
    let verified = engine.verify(&generated, file)?;
    println!(
        "Lean checked {} obligations in {}",
        verified.theorem_names.len(),
        verified.path.display()
    );
    println!(
        "Input hypotheses: {} (theorem remains conditional)",
        verified.assumptions.len()
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stage4_gpu.rs
//! Stage 4 executable GPU path: one Rust module graph, CPU oracle and CUDA.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    Domain, GpuEngine, MathContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NeuralModule, NodeId, PortContract,
    Shape, Tensor,
};

struct ReluLayer {
    contract: MathContract,
}

impl NeuralModule for ReluLayer {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "relu_layer"
    }

    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
        &self.contract
    }

    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.relu(inputs[0])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![2, 3])?;
    let x = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![-3.0f32, -0.0, 0.5, 2.0, 4.0, 7.0])?;
    let y = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![2.0f32, 3.0, -1.0, 0.5, 2.0, 4.0])?;

    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let input_x = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let input_y = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let relu = ReluLayer {
        contract: MathContract::new(
            vec![PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite)],
            PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite),
        ),
    };
    let active = graph.apply_module(&relu, &[input_x])?;
    let flattened = graph.reshape(active, Shape::new(vec![6])?)?;
    let restored = graph.reshape(flattened, shape)?;
    let product = graph.mul(restored, input_y)?;
    let result = graph.add(product, active)?;

    // Independent host reference, using the stage-2 Tensor operations.
    let cpu_active = x.relu();
    let cpu_result = cpu_active.mul(&y)?.add(&cpu_active)?;

    let engine = GpuEngine::default();
    let program = engine.compile(&graph, result)?;
    let output = engine.execute(
        &program,
        &[(input_x, x), (input_y, y)],
        Path::new("target/verineural/gpu-stage4"),
    )?;

    for (&actual, &expected) in output.values().iter().zip(cpu_result.values()) {
        if actual.to_bits() != expected.to_bits() {
            return Err(
                format!("GPU differs from CPU: actual={actual:?} expected={expected:?}").into(),
            );
        }
    }
    println!(
        "GPU execution matched CPU for {} FP32 values",
        output.values().len()
    );
    println!("LLVM IR and PTX: target/verineural/gpu-stage4/");
    println!("Scope: numerical validation, not a proof of the GPU machine code.");
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stage5_cert.rs
//! Stage 5: one Rust graph, Lean evidence, GPU execution and integrity report.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    CertificateEngine, Domain, MathContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NeuralModule, NodeId,
    PortContract, Shape, Tensor,
};

struct ReluLayer {
    contract: MathContract,
}

impl NeuralModule for ReluLayer {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "relu_layer"
    }

    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
        &self.contract
    }

    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.relu(inputs[0])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![2, 3])?;
    let x = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![-3.0f32, -0.0, 0.5, 2.0, 4.0, 7.0])?;
    let y = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![2.0f32, 3.0, -1.0, 0.5, 2.0, 4.0])?;

    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let input_x = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let input_y = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let relu = ReluLayer {
        contract: MathContract::new(
            vec![PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite)],
            PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite),
        ),
    };
    let active = graph.apply_module(&relu, &[input_x])?;
    let flattened = graph.reshape(active, Shape::new(vec![6])?)?;
    let restored = graph.reshape(flattened, shape)?;
    let product = graph.mul(restored, input_y)?;
    let result = graph.add(product, active)?;

    // Independent host reference, using the stage-2 Tensor operations.
    let cpu_active = x.relu();
    let cpu_result = cpu_active.mul(&y)?.add(&cpu_active)?;

    let engine = CertificateEngine::default();
    let report = engine.run(
        &graph,
        result,
        &[(input_x, x), (input_y, y)],
        &cpu_result,
        Path::new("target/verineural/stage5"),
    )?;
    // Check the saved file hashes and replay Lean verification.
    engine.verify_bundle(&report.directory)?;
    println!(
        "Lean: {} theorems; GPU vs CPU: {} identical FP32 bit patterns",
        report.theorem_count, report.compared_fp32_values
    );
    println!("Report: {}/report.json", report.directory.display());
    println!("SHA256SUMS sha256: {}", report.manifest_sha256);
    println!(
        "Evidence: mathematical/composition=proven (ideal Int), numerical=validated, compilation=trusted, FP32/machine code=unsupported"
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stage5_verify.rs
//! Recheck a saved Stage 5 bundle without requiring a GPU run.
//! Pin the SHA256SUMS digest from the original run separately if authenticity matters.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::CertificateEngine;

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let dir = Path::new("target/verineural/stage5");
    let engine = CertificateEngine::default();
    match std::env::var("VERINEURAL_STAGE5_SHA256") {
        Ok(expected) => {
            engine.verify_bundle_with_digest(dir, &expected)?;
            println!("Pinned manifest digest: PASS");
        }
        Err(std::env::VarError::NotPresent) => {
            engine.verify_bundle(dir)?;
            println!("Unpinned manifest: integrity only, provenance NOT verified");
        }
        Err(error) => return Err(Box::new(error)),
    }
    println!("Bundle hash consistency: PASS");
    println!("Saved Lean source: rechecked by Lean 4");
    println!("No PTX semantic-preservation or GPU execution proof is implied.");
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stage6_ffn.rs
//! Stage 6: Residual FFN from one Rust graph to Lean + NVIDIA GPU + evidence.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{CertificateEngine, Domain, NeuralGraph, ResidualFfn, Shape, Tensor};

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![2, 2])?;
    let x = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![1.0_f32, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0])?;
    let w1 = Tensor::new(Shape::new(vec![2, 3])?, vec![1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0])?;
    let b1 = Tensor::new(Shape::new(vec![3])?, vec![-1.0, 0.0, 1.0])?;
    let w2 = Tensor::new(Shape::new(vec![3, 2])?, vec![1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0])?;
    let b2 = Tensor::new(Shape::new(vec![2])?, vec![0.0, 1.0])?;

    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let x_id = graph.input(shape, Domain::Finite);
    let w1_id = graph.input(w1.shape().clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let b1_id = graph.input(b1.shape().clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let w2_id = graph.input(w2.shape().clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let b2_id = graph.input(b2.shape().clone(), Domain::Finite);

    let ffn = ResidualFfn::new(2, 2, 3)?;
    let output = graph.apply_module(&ffn, &[x_id, w1_id, b1_id, w2_id, b2_id])?;
    // CPU oracle is independently expressed in terms of concrete Tensor ops.
    let activated = x.matmul(&w1)?.bias_add(&b1)?.relu();
    let projected = activated.matmul(&w2)?.bias_add(&b2)?;
    let cpu = x.add(&projected)?;

    let engine = CertificateEngine::default();
    let report = engine.run(
        &graph,
        output,
        &[
            (x_id, x),
            (w1_id, w1),
            (b1_id, b1),
            (w2_id, w2),
            (b2_id, b2),
        ],
        &cpu,
        Path::new("target/verineural/stage6"),
    )?;
    engine.verify_bundle(&report.directory)?;
    println!(
        "Stage 6: Lean checked {} obligations, GPU matched {} CPU FP32 values",
        report.theorem_count, report.compared_fp32_values
    );
    println!("Report: {}/report.json", report.directory.display());
    println!("Pin manifest digest externally: {}", report.manifest_sha256);
    println!("Lean covers ideal Int/model obligations, not f32 or GPU machine code.");
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stage7_benchmark.rs
//! Stage 7 workload experiment: reproducible graph replay timings, not a GPU proof.
//! Run separately from the hash-pinned Stage 7 evidence example.

use std::error::Error;
use std::io;
use std::path::Path;
use std::time::Instant;

use verineural::{
    Domain, GpuEngine, GpuError, GpuExecution, GpuLaunchConfig, NeuralGraph, NodeId, ReluFusion,
    Shape, Tensor,
};

const COLUMNS: usize = 256;
const ELEMENT_COUNTS: [usize; 4] = [1_024, 16_384, 262_144, 1_048_576];
const SAMPLES: usize = 5;
const WARMUP: usize = 25;
const REPLAYS: usize = 1_000;

fn dataset(rows: usize, variant: usize) -> Result<[Tensor<f32>; 3], Box<dyn Error>> {
    let elements = rows * COLUMNS;
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![rows, COLUMNS])?;
    let x = (0..elements)
        .map(|i| match (i + variant) % 32 {
            0 => -0.0f32,
            1 => 0.0,
            2 => f32::MIN_POSITIVE,
            3 => -f32::MIN_POSITIVE,
            _ => ((i % 17) as i32 - 8) as f32 * 0.25 + variant as f32,
        })
        .collect();
    let y = (0..elements)
        .map(|i| ((i * 3 + variant * 5) % 13) as f32 * 0.25 - 1.5)
        .collect();
    let bias = (0..COLUMNS)
        .map(|i| ((i + variant * 3) % 11) as f32 * 0.125 - 0.625)
        .collect();
    Ok([
        Tensor::new(shape.clone(), x)?,
        Tensor::new(shape, y)?,
        Tensor::new(Shape::new(vec![COLUMNS])?, bias)?,
    ])
}

fn inputs(ids: [NodeId; 3], tensors: &[Tensor<f32>; 3]) -> [(NodeId, Tensor<f32>); 3] {
    [
        (ids[0], tensors[0].clone()),
        (ids[1], tensors[1].clone()),
        (ids[2], tensors[2].clone()),
    ]
}

fn reference(t: &[Tensor<f32>; 3]) -> Result<Tensor<f32>, Box<dyn Error>> {
    Ok(t[0].add(&t[1])?.bias_add(&t[2])?.relu())
}

fn check_bits(label: &str, observed: &Tensor<f32>, expected: &Tensor<f32>) -> io::Result<()> {
    if observed.shape() != expected.shape() {
        return Err(io::Error::other(format!("{label}: shape mismatch")));
    }
    for (i, (&actual, &cpu)) in observed.values().iter().zip(expected.values()).enumerate() {
        if actual.to_bits() != cpu.to_bits() {
            return Err(io::Error::other(format!(
                "{label}: FP32 mismatch at {i}: GPU={:08x}, CPU={:08x}",
                actual.to_bits(),
                cpu.to_bits()
            )));
        }
    }
    Ok(())
}

fn summary(samples: &mut [f64]) -> (f64, f64, f64) {
    samples.sort_by(f64::total_cmp);
    (
        samples[0],
        samples[samples.len() / 2],
        samples[samples.len() - 1],
    )
}

/// Wall-clock time for a full prepared execution with fresh H2D inputs and
/// D2H output. CPU reference comparisons are performed *after* this interval.
fn full_cycle(
    exec: &mut GpuExecution,
    inputs: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)],
) -> Result<(f64, Tensor<f32>), GpuError> {
    let started = Instant::now();
    exec.update_inputs(inputs)?;
    exec.replay()?;
    let result = exec.read_output()?;
    Ok((started.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1_000_000.0, result))
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn Error>> {
    let baseline =
        GpuEngine::default().with_launch_config(GpuLaunchConfig::new(256, ReluFusion::Disabled)?);
    let fused = GpuEngine::default()
        .with_launch_config(GpuLaunchConfig::new(256, ReluFusion::Experimental)?);
    let root = Path::new("target/verineural/stage7-workload");
    println!(
        "CUDA Graph workload experiment: {SAMPLES} series, {WARMUP} warmup + {REPLAYS} measured per series"
    );
    println!(
        "Results are CUDA-event stream replay intervals in microseconds, not GPU-kernel-only latency"
    );
    println!(
        "elements | baseline min/median/max us | fused min/median/max us | fused/baseline median"
    );

    for elements in ELEMENT_COUNTS {
        let rows = elements / COLUMNS;
        let shape = Shape::new(vec![rows, COLUMNS])?;
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let xid = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
        let yid = graph.input(shape, Domain::Finite);
        let bid = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![COLUMNS])?, Domain::Finite);
        let added = graph.add(xid, yid)?;
        let biased = graph.bias_add(added, bid)?;
        let output = graph.relu(biased)?;
        let ids = [xid, yid, bid];

        let plan_a = baseline.compile(&graph, output)?;
        let plan_b = fused.compile(&graph, output)?;
        if plan_b.removed_kernel_count() != 2 {
            return Err(io::Error::other("chain fusion did not remove two kernels").into());
        }
        let first = dataset(rows, 0)?;
        let first_inputs = inputs(ids, &first);
        let first_expected = reference(&first)?;
        let path = root.join(elements.to_string());
        let start_a = Instant::now();
        let mut exec_a = baseline.prepare(&plan_a, &first_inputs, &path.join("baseline"))?;
        let setup_a = start_a.elapsed();
        let start_b = Instant::now();
        let mut exec_b = fused.prepare(&plan_b, &first_inputs, &path.join("fused"))?;
        let setup_b = start_b.elapsed();
        println!(
            "setup {elements:8}: baseline {:.3} ms, fused {:.3} ms (includes llc, JIT, allocations, graph capture)",
            setup_a.as_secs_f64() * 1_000.0,
            setup_b.as_secs_f64() * 1_000.0,
        );

        exec_a.replay()?;
        exec_b.replay()?;
        check_bits("initial baseline", &exec_a.read_output()?, &first_expected)?;
        check_bits("initial fused", &exec_b.read_output()?, &first_expected)?;

        // Rebind new input values to both *existing* CUgraphExec instances.
        let second = dataset(rows, 1)?;
        let second_inputs = inputs(ids, &second);
        let second_expected = reference(&second)?;
        if first_expected.values() == second_expected.values() {
            return Err(io::Error::other("test datasets produced identical outputs").into());
        }
        exec_a.update_inputs(&second_inputs)?;
        exec_b.update_inputs(&second_inputs)?;
        exec_a.replay()?;
        exec_b.replay()?;
        check_bits("updated baseline", &exec_a.read_output()?, &second_expected)?;
        check_bits("updated fused", &exec_b.read_output()?, &second_expected)?;

        // Input validation is all-or-nothing: a rejected batch must not have
        // modified the previously accepted device inputs.
        let mut invalid = second_inputs.clone();
        let mut data = invalid[0].1.values().to_vec();
        data[0] = f32::NAN;
        invalid[0].1 = Tensor::new(Shape::new(vec![rows, COLUMNS])?, data)?;
        if !matches!(
            exec_a.update_inputs(&invalid),
            Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(_))
        ) || !matches!(
            exec_b.update_inputs(&invalid),
            Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(_))
        ) {
            return Err(io::Error::other("non-finite input update was not rejected").into());
        }
        exec_a.replay()?;
        exec_b.replay()?;
        check_bits(
            "rejected update baseline",
            &exec_a.read_output()?,
            &second_expected,
        )?;
        check_bits(
            "rejected update fused",
            &exec_b.read_output()?,
            &second_expected,
        )?;

        // Alternate measurement order to reduce systematic drift bias.
        let mut times_a = Vec::with_capacity(SAMPLES);
        let mut times_b = Vec::with_capacity(SAMPLES);
        for trial in 0..SAMPLES {
            let (a, b) = if trial % 2 == 0 {
                (
                    exec_a.benchmark(WARMUP, REPLAYS)?,
                    exec_b.benchmark(WARMUP, REPLAYS)?,
                )
            } else {
                let b = exec_b.benchmark(WARMUP, REPLAYS)?;
                let a = exec_a.benchmark(WARMUP, REPLAYS)?;
                (a, b)
            };
            times_a.push(a.average().as_secs_f64() * 1_000_000.0);
            times_b.push(b.average().as_secs_f64() * 1_000_000.0);
        }
        let (amin, amed, amax) = summary(&mut times_a);
        let (bmin, bmed, bmax) = summary(&mut times_b);
        println!(
            "{elements:8} | {amin:7.3}/{amed:7.3}/{amax:7.3} | {bmin:7.3}/{bmed:7.3}/{bmax:7.3} | {ratio:.3}x",
            ratio = bmed / amed
        );

        // Replay-only GPU-event timings above intentionally omit transfers.
        // Contrast them with the actual host-observed input -> output cycle.
        let mut full_a = Vec::with_capacity(SAMPLES);
        let mut full_b = Vec::with_capacity(SAMPLES);
        for trial in 0..SAMPLES {
            if trial % 2 == 0 {
                let (us, result) = full_cycle(&mut exec_a, &second_inputs)?;
                full_a.push(us);
                check_bits("full-cycle baseline", &result, &second_expected)?;
                let (us, result) = full_cycle(&mut exec_b, &second_inputs)?;
                full_b.push(us);
                check_bits("full-cycle fused", &result, &second_expected)?;
            } else {
                let (us, result) = full_cycle(&mut exec_b, &second_inputs)?;
                full_b.push(us);
                check_bits("full-cycle fused", &result, &second_expected)?;
                let (us, result) = full_cycle(&mut exec_a, &second_inputs)?;
                full_a.push(us);
                check_bits("full-cycle baseline", &result, &second_expected)?;
            }
        }
        let (famin, famed, famax) = summary(&mut full_a);
        let (fbmin, fbmed, fbmax) = summary(&mut full_b);
        println!(
            "full cycle:  {famin:7.3}/{famed:7.3}/{famax:7.3} | {fbmin:7.3}/{fbmed:7.3}/{fbmax:7.3} | {ratio:.3}x (H2D + graph + D2H + synchronization)",
            ratio = fbmed / famed
        );
    }
    println!(
        "Each size verified by bitwise CPU comparison before and after graph input replacement"
    );
    println!(
        "Including signed zeros and minimum normal values does not prove general IEEE-754 equivalence"
    );
    println!("Full-cycle wall time includes pinned staging reuse and synchronous result readback");
    println!("Profilers perturb short CUDA Graph workloads; compare performance without nsys");
    println!("No FP32, PTX, machine code or GPU memory-safety proof is implied.");
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stage7_fusion.rs
//! Stage 7: opt-in Relu fusion and controlled CUDA launch comparison.
//!
//! Both modes compile from the same Rust graph, check Lean, and compare every
//! returned f32 bit pattern against the same independent CPU reference.
//! The experimental ideal-Int fusion theorem is checked separately; LLVM/PTX
//! and floating-point equivalence are not formally established.
use std::fs;
use std::io;
use std::path::Path;
use std::process::Command;

use verineural::{
    CertificateEngine, Domain, GpuEngine, GpuLaunchConfig, LeanProofEngine, NeuralGraph,
    ReluFusion, Shape, Tensor,
};

const STAGE7_ARTIFACTS: [&str; 5] = [
    "fusion.lean",
    "memory_baseline.lean",
    "memory_fused.lean",
    "baseline/SHA256SUMS",
    "fused/SHA256SUMS",
];

fn digest(path: &Path) -> Result<String, Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let output = Command::new("sha256sum").arg(path).output()?;
    if !output.status.success() {
        return Err(io::Error::other("sha256sum failed").into());
    }
    let text = String::from_utf8(output.stdout)?;
    let hash = text.split_whitespace().next().unwrap_or("");
    if hash.len() != 64 || !hash.bytes().all(|b| b.is_ascii_hexdigit()) {
        return Err(io::Error::other("invalid sha256sum digest").into());
    }
    Ok(hash.to_owned())
}

/// No GPU run: verify all three pinned sub-artifacts, and rerun Lean.
fn verify_stage7(root: &Path) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let manifest = root.join("SHA256SUMS");
    if let Ok(expected) = std::env::var("VERINEURAL_STAGE7_SHA256") {
        if digest(&manifest)? != expected {
            return Err(io::Error::other("Stage 7 pinned digest mismatch").into());
        }
    }
    let check = Command::new("sha256sum")
        .current_dir(root)
        .args(["--check", "SHA256SUMS"])
        .output()?;
    if !check.status.success() {
        return Err(io::Error::other(format!(
            "Stage 7 manifest rejected: {}",
            String::from_utf8_lossy(&check.stderr)
        ))
        .into());
    }
    let proof = LeanProofEngine::default();
    proof.check_file(&root.join("fusion.lean"))?;
    proof.check_file(&root.join("memory_baseline.lean"))?;
    proof.check_file(&root.join("memory_fused.lean"))?;
    for name in ["baseline", "fused"] {
        CertificateEngine::default().verify_bundle(&root.join(name))?;
    }
    Ok(())
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let root = Path::new("target/verineural/stage7");
    if std::env::args().any(|a| a == "--verify") {
        verify_stage7(root)?;
        println!("Stage 7: hashes and all saved Lean sources verified (no GPU replay)");
        return Ok(());
    }
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![2, 3])?;
    let x = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![-3.0_f32, 0.0, 1.0, 2.0, -2.0, 5.0])?;
    let y = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![0.5_f32, 2.0, -2.0, 1.0, 3.0, 0.0])?;
    let bias = Tensor::new(Shape::new(vec![3])?, vec![1.0_f32, -1.0, 2.0])?;

    // A user-defined composition rather than a prescribed LLM architecture.
    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let xid = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let yid = graph.input(shape, Domain::Finite);
    let bid = graph.input(bias.shape().clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let mixture = graph.add(xid, yid)?;
    let biased = graph.bias_add(mixture, bid)?;
    let output = graph.relu(biased)?;
    let reference = x.add(&y)?.bias_add(&bias)?.relu();
    let inputs = [(xid, x), (yid, y), (bid, bias)];
    fs::create_dir_all(root)?;
    // Fail closed: a previous success manifest must not survive a bad rerun.
    for name in [
        "SHA256SUMS",
        "fusion.lean",
        "memory_baseline.lean",
        "memory_fused.lean",
        "baseline/SHA256SUMS",
        "baseline/report.json",
        "fused/SHA256SUMS",
        "fused/report.json",
    ] {
        match fs::remove_file(root.join(name)) {
            Ok(()) => {}
            Err(err) if err.kind() == io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {}
            Err(err) => return Err(err.into()),
        }
    }

    // Keep launch geometry identical so fusion is the measured variable.
    let baseline =
        GpuEngine::default().with_launch_config(GpuLaunchConfig::new(256, ReluFusion::Disabled)?);
    let fused = GpuEngine::default()
        .with_launch_config(GpuLaunchConfig::new(256, ReluFusion::Experimental)?);
    let unoptimized_plan = baseline.compile(&graph, output)?;
    let fused_plan = fused.compile(&graph, output)?;
    if fused_plan.fused_pointwise_chains().len() != 1 || fused_plan.removed_kernel_count() != 2 {
        return Err(io::Error::other(
            "expected Add -> BiasAdd -> Relu to remove exactly two kernels",
        )
        .into());
    }

    // Check the mathematical rewrite using the real Lean executable.
    // The proof is not a proof of code generation or IEEE-754 equivalence.
    let fusion_lean = root.join("fusion.lean");
    let source = fused_plan
        .fusion_lean_source()
        .ok_or_else(|| io::Error::other("no fusion lemma emitted"))?;
    fs::write(&fusion_lean, source)?;
    let proof = LeanProofEngine::default();
    proof.check_file(&fusion_lean)?;
    // Both lowering variants get kernel-by-kernel memory-layout obligations
    // with concrete Rust IR extents. These are natural-number indexing lemmas,
    // not PTX or machine-memory proofs.
    for (name, program) in [
        ("memory_baseline.lean", &unoptimized_plan),
        ("memory_fused.lean", &fused_plan),
    ] {
        let source = program.memory_lean_source()?;
        let path = root.join(name);
        fs::write(&path, source)?;
        proof.check_file(&path)?;
    }

    // Evidence generation still performs its own one-shot replay and bitwise CPU check.
    let baseline_cert = CertificateEngine::new(LeanProofEngine::default(), baseline.clone());
    let baseline_report =
        baseline_cert.run(&graph, output, &inputs, &reference, &root.join("baseline"))?;
    baseline_cert.verify_bundle(&baseline_report.directory)?;

    let fused_cert = CertificateEngine::new(LeanProofEngine::default(), fused.clone());
    let fused_report = fused_cert.run(&graph, output, &inputs, &reference, &root.join("fused"))?;
    fused_cert.verify_bundle(&fused_report.directory)?;

    // Benchmark only an already instantiated CUgraphExec. CUDA events exclude
    // Lean, LLVM, context/JIT setup, allocations and host transfers.
    let benchmark_root = Path::new("target/verineural/stage7-benchmark");
    match fs::remove_dir_all(benchmark_root) {
        Ok(()) => {}
        Err(err) if err.kind() == io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {}
        Err(err) => return Err(err.into()),
    }
    let mut baseline_execution =
        baseline.prepare(&unoptimized_plan, &inputs, &benchmark_root.join("baseline"))?;
    let mut fused_execution = fused.prepare(&fused_plan, &inputs, &benchmark_root.join("fused"))?;
    let baseline_benchmark = baseline_execution.benchmark(25, 1000)?;
    let fused_benchmark = fused_execution.benchmark(25, 1000)?;

    for (label, actual) in [
        ("baseline", baseline_execution.read_output()?),
        ("fused", fused_execution.read_output()?),
    ] {
        for (index, (&gpu, &cpu)) in actual.values().iter().zip(reference.values()).enumerate() {
            if gpu.to_bits() != cpu.to_bits() {
                return Err(io::Error::other(format!(
                    "{label} benchmark output mismatch at {index}: GPU={:08x} CPU={:08x}",
                    gpu.to_bits(),
                    cpu.to_bits()
                ))
                .into());
            }
        }
    }

    let count_kernels = |text: &str| text.matches("define ptx_kernel void").count();
    let hashes = Command::new("sha256sum")
        .current_dir(root)
        .args(STAGE7_ARTIFACTS)
        .output()?;
    if !hashes.status.success() {
        return Err(io::Error::other("Stage 7 sha256sum generation failed").into());
    }
    fs::write(root.join("SHA256SUMS"), hashes.stdout)?;
    if let Err(err) = verify_stage7(root) {
        let _ = fs::remove_file(root.join("SHA256SUMS"));
        return Err(err);
    }

    println!(
        "Stage 7: kernels {} -> {}, guarded fusions {}",
        count_kernels(unoptimized_plan.llvm_ir()),
        count_kernels(fused_plan.llvm_ir()),
        fused_plan.fused_relus().len(),
    );
    println!("Launch: baseline/fused both 256 threads per block");
    println!(
        "CPU comparisons: baseline {} / fused {} identical f32 values",
        baseline_report.compared_fp32_values, fused_report.compared_fp32_values
    );
    println!("Lean ideal-Int rule checked: {}", fusion_lean.display());
    println!(
        "CUDA-event graph replay: baseline {:?} total / {:.3} us avg; fused {:?} total / {:.3} us avg",
        baseline_benchmark.elapsed(),
        baseline_benchmark.average().as_secs_f64() * 1_000_000.0,
        fused_benchmark.elapsed(),
        fused_benchmark.average().as_secs_f64() * 1_000_000.0,
    );
    println!(
        "Benchmark protocol: {} warmup + {} measured replays, one CUgraphExec per mode",
        baseline_benchmark.warmup_launches(),
        baseline_benchmark.measured_launches(),
    );
    println!(
        "SHA256SUMS digests: baseline {}, fused {}",
        baseline_report.manifest_sha256, fused_report.manifest_sha256
    );
    println!(
        "Pinned Stage 7 SHA256SUMS digest: {}",
        digest(&root.join("SHA256SUMS"))?
    );
    println!("Recheck without a GPU: task verify-gpu-stage7");
    println!(
        "Stage 7 manifest covers fusion + baseline/fused memory Lean obligations and both Stage 5 evidence manifests."
    );
    println!("No certified PTX/FP32/machine-code equivalence is claimed.");
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stage8_exact.rs
//! Stage 8: exact-integer ranges plus concrete fractional dyadic RNE/epsilon
//! traces. Rust input guards -> Lean range/error lemmas -> baseline/fused CUDA
//! Graph -> independent integer oracles -> SHA-256 evidence.
//! The LLVM/PTX/JIT/GPU link remains trusted rather than formally proved.

use std::error::Error;
use std::fs;
use std::io;
use std::path::Path;
use std::process::Command;

use verineural::{
    Domain, ExactFp32Plan, Fp32SpecialExpected, GpuEngine, GpuLaunchConfig, LeanProofEngine,
    MathContract, NeuralGraph, NeuralModule, NodeId, PortContract, ReluFusion, ResidualAdd,
    ResidualFfn, RneFp32Plan, RneRangePlan, RneThresholdSide, Shape, Tensor, TranslationPlan,
    audit_fp32_ptx, special_mul_bias_relu_boundary, subnormal_add_exact_bits,
    subnormal_mul_rne_bits, subnormal_relu_bits,
};

